WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:06.882
[theme song playing]

00:06.965 --> 00:09.885
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:11.136 --> 00:14.723
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.312
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.395 --> 00:23.690
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:26.902
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.694 --> 00:30.697
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.615 --> 00:35.702
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:35.786 --> 00:39.540
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.623 --> 00:43.544
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.627 --> 00:44.586
[song concludes]

00:44.670 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:47.506 --> 00:48.590
[in Korean] I…

00:50.884 --> 00:52.386
I liked you too.

00:53.220 --> 00:56.265
[gentle music playing]

01:05.649 --> 01:07.150
Ho-su.

01:07.234 --> 01:10.279
I liked you too!

01:11.238 --> 01:13.240
You're drunk.

01:13.323 --> 01:15.033
Let's pretend you didn't say any of that.

01:15.117 --> 01:16.159
[Mi-ji] Hey, Ho-su.

01:16.785 --> 01:18.620
Why are you always so difficult?

01:18.704 --> 01:19.955
What's going on?

01:20.038 --> 01:21.707
Just say it.

01:21.790 --> 01:25.085
Who do you like right now?

01:25.919 --> 01:27.129
I also…

01:29.673 --> 01:34.636
EPISODE 6
THE SILENT, EVER-PRESENT FOOL

01:34.720 --> 01:36.513
[music concludes]

01:37.806 --> 01:39.433
[exhales]

01:45.188 --> 01:46.898
What the…

01:47.399 --> 01:48.942
Why am I here?

01:49.735 --> 01:51.862
[lively quirky music playing]

01:52.696 --> 01:53.780
[Ho-su] Mi-rae.

01:54.281 --> 01:56.116
I liked you too! Darn it. Yes, you!

01:56.199 --> 01:57.743
[gasps] Holy crap!

01:57.826 --> 02:00.912
Duson-- The person you like…
Hey, just say it.

02:00.996 --> 02:01.872
I also…

02:01.955 --> 02:04.458
Oh! Oh, darn it.

02:04.541 --> 02:07.628
Why did I say those things as Mi-rae?

02:07.711 --> 02:09.087
But wait.

02:09.171 --> 02:10.088
"Also"?

02:10.172 --> 02:12.549
Did he mean, "I also like you"?

02:12.633 --> 02:15.010
Jeez. What happened after that?

02:15.093 --> 02:16.678
Come on, think!

02:16.762 --> 02:18.722
- [door lock beeping]
- [gasps]

02:20.057 --> 02:22.059
- [door lock chimes]
- [door opens]

02:24.227 --> 02:26.146
- [door closes]
- [Mi-ji clears throat]

02:26.229 --> 02:27.397
[music concludes]

02:29.399 --> 02:30.484
You're up.

02:30.567 --> 02:31.652
Yes.

02:33.945 --> 02:36.198
How did I end up sleeping here last night?

02:36.281 --> 02:38.700
You should've sent me home if I was drunk.

02:38.784 --> 02:40.327
Do you really think I didn't try to?

02:42.746 --> 02:45.290
Anyway, sorry for the trouble.

02:45.874 --> 02:46.792
My bad.

02:49.378 --> 02:50.253
Here, take this.

02:50.337 --> 02:51.630
[soft quirky music playing]

02:51.713 --> 02:55.425
I never thought I'd buy a hangover cure
first thing in the morning.

02:56.301 --> 02:58.345
[Mi-ji] Why is he being low-key nice?

02:58.428 --> 03:00.597
Is it because I said I liked him?

03:00.681 --> 03:02.224
- What?
- [Mi-ji] Hey.

03:02.849 --> 03:04.226
Let me ask you something.

03:05.060 --> 03:07.270
Did I do anything stupid last night?

03:07.354 --> 03:08.355
Like what?

03:08.980 --> 03:09.981
When I get drunk,

03:10.607 --> 03:12.943
I say things I don't mean,
but I sound like I do.

03:13.026 --> 03:15.237
It's gotten me into trouble before.

03:15.320 --> 03:17.072
So I just wanted to check.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.949
I'm not sure what you mean exactly.

03:19.658 --> 03:21.910
You said a lot last night.

03:24.329 --> 03:28.875
You know, things like outrageous lies

03:28.959 --> 03:30.711
or maybe a love confession.

03:30.794 --> 03:33.004
If I said I liked you or whatever,

03:33.088 --> 03:36.675
please don't take it the wrong way
and make things awkward between us.

03:37.300 --> 03:39.261
So you remember up to that part.

03:39.845 --> 03:43.140
Even if I said more after that,

03:43.223 --> 03:44.766
I didn't mean any of it.

03:44.850 --> 03:46.601
I don't see you that way at all.

03:46.685 --> 03:50.147
You're just another person to me.
Maybe an old classmate at best.

03:50.230 --> 03:51.148
That's it.

03:51.231 --> 03:53.316
[Ho-su] Looks like
you don't remember much after that.

03:53.400 --> 03:54.651
Don't worry.

03:54.735 --> 03:55.819
What?

03:55.902 --> 03:59.281
I've already sorted things out,
so you don't need to worry.

04:02.492 --> 04:05.245
Well, then… Okay.

04:07.622 --> 04:10.751
Wait. Sorted what out exactly?

04:10.834 --> 04:13.253
What else happened after that?

04:14.421 --> 04:15.380
What now?

04:16.047 --> 04:20.302
I think we need to clear up some things.

04:20.385 --> 04:23.972
Even if it's a little embarrassing,
we should both know what happened.

04:24.055 --> 04:26.683
That way, if there's anything to explain,
we can talk it out.

04:26.767 --> 04:28.226
- [Ho-su] Mi-rae.
- What?

04:29.686 --> 04:30.979
Shouldn't you go to work?

04:33.315 --> 04:34.441
[music concludes]

04:35.358 --> 04:36.276
[Mi-ji] My phone.

04:36.359 --> 04:38.904
Hey, what time is it?
Don't you have a clock?

04:38.987 --> 04:40.614
[gasps] Holy crap!

04:42.574 --> 04:44.826
[soft pensive music playing]

04:44.910 --> 04:47.829
EASY MORNING
HANGOVER CURE

04:48.789 --> 04:49.664
[door opens]

04:56.004 --> 04:57.631
Yu Mi-rae isn't here yet?

04:58.590 --> 05:00.133
- [music fades]
- She went to the restroom.

05:00.217 --> 05:02.093
She's never around when you need her.

05:03.136 --> 05:04.304
I need some copies made.

05:04.387 --> 05:05.680
I can do it.

05:07.474 --> 05:08.683
The copying, I mean.

05:09.935 --> 05:11.228
Oh, sure.

05:13.855 --> 05:15.106
[quirky music playing]

05:15.190 --> 05:17.567
I don't have my phone and wallet.

05:17.651 --> 05:19.486
- Where are they?
- I got them. Here.

05:19.569 --> 05:21.071
[Mi-ji] Thank you.

05:21.154 --> 05:22.197
Oh! My bag.

05:22.280 --> 05:24.241
- I'll drop it off for you later.
- What?

05:24.324 --> 05:26.201
- Or else they'll know you're late.
- Really?

05:26.284 --> 05:29.204
- Okay, then.
- I called a cab. It's waiting downstairs.

05:29.287 --> 05:32.582
What? Thanks. I'll get going.

05:34.793 --> 05:36.044
[door lock chimes]

05:38.046 --> 05:39.172
[door lock chimes]

05:39.256 --> 05:40.882
[quirky music continues]

05:52.185 --> 05:54.479
- [Gyeong-min] What are you doing?
- Hi, Mr. Shin.

05:54.563 --> 05:56.731
- [music concludes]
- Making your bathroom break public?

05:56.815 --> 05:58.900
- Mind your manners.
- Yes, sir.

05:58.984 --> 06:00.986
- [Tae-i] Mr. Shin.
- [in English] Thank you.

06:01.069 --> 06:03.154
[in Korean] Sorry you had to do
someone else's work.

06:03.238 --> 06:05.615
- If you're ready, let's go.
- [Gyeong-min] Yes, sir.

06:05.699 --> 06:06.992
Where are you going?

06:07.075 --> 06:08.535
You're coming too.

06:08.618 --> 06:10.954
Me? Where…

06:11.037 --> 06:12.080
Me?

06:16.167 --> 06:19.337
We've secured
about 62% of the land so far.

06:19.421 --> 06:22.090
The key challenge
is still the Aesim Shopping Center,

06:22.173 --> 06:24.634
so we're in talks
with the merchants' association…

06:24.718 --> 06:25.927
Yes?

06:26.553 --> 06:29.639
What about the buildings next to it?
How many have we secured?

06:30.265 --> 06:31.474
Uh…

06:31.558 --> 06:34.644
Well, as of now…

06:35.186 --> 06:37.105
So far we've secured…

06:37.731 --> 06:39.399
- It's 79%.
- [intriguing music playing]

06:39.482 --> 06:40.567
It's 79%.

06:40.650 --> 06:44.112
I think securing the sites next to it
will be even more challenging.

06:44.738 --> 06:47.866
What kind of residential units
are in the other buildings?

06:47.949 --> 06:50.744
The residential units…

06:51.286 --> 06:54.664
The area is 83.6% general residential,
all with less than seven floors…

06:54.748 --> 06:57.834
I'm not asking for percentages.

06:57.918 --> 06:59.753
What kind of housing are they?

06:59.836 --> 07:01.504
[Gyeong-min clears throat] Right.

07:02.255 --> 07:04.883
- Well…
- There are two single-family homes,

07:04.966 --> 07:06.718
and the rest are multi-unit buildings.

07:06.801 --> 07:08.511
That's what I thought.

07:08.595 --> 07:10.347
I figured there'd be multi-unit buildings.

07:10.430 --> 07:11.598
[mouths] I see.

07:11.681 --> 07:15.143
Multiple owners means more conflict
and more chances of a holdout.

07:15.226 --> 07:17.520
Will everyone be moved out
before construction?

07:17.604 --> 07:21.524
We're preparing a meeting with
the residents to keep things on schedule.

07:21.608 --> 07:24.069
If a meeting were enough,
I wouldn't be worried.

07:24.152 --> 07:25.946
Do you really think it's possible?

07:28.239 --> 07:30.992
If it's the multi-unit buildings
you're worried about,

07:31.076 --> 07:33.870
I already checked.
They're in the process of moving out.

07:35.580 --> 07:37.791
You went there just to check?

07:37.874 --> 07:39.668
- [Mi-ji] Not really.
- [music concludes]

07:39.751 --> 07:42.420
I'm in charge of a restaurant nearby,

07:42.504 --> 07:44.130
so I just happened to notice.

07:44.214 --> 07:45.632
[CEO] A restaurant?

07:45.715 --> 07:48.760
Wait, are you in charge
of Rosa Restaurant?

07:49.469 --> 07:50.345
Yes.

07:50.428 --> 07:51.638
What's your name?

07:51.721 --> 07:53.056
Oh, I'm…

07:55.558 --> 07:58.353
I'm Yu Mi-rae, a Senior Specialist.

07:59.479 --> 08:01.773
[mellow quirky music playing]

08:04.484 --> 08:06.111
[mellow quirky music continues]

08:08.571 --> 08:09.656
[sighs contently]

08:09.739 --> 08:10.824
NEW HQ PROJECT REPORT

08:10.907 --> 08:13.868
So all that work
wasn't for nothing after all.

08:18.081 --> 08:19.124
Hmm?

08:29.509 --> 08:30.593
Jeez…

08:35.598 --> 08:38.560
SORRY I MADE YOU GO THROUGH THIS ALONE
BUT I'M ALWAYS THINKING OF YOU - SY

08:38.643 --> 08:39.894
[music fades]

08:40.603 --> 08:41.688
[employee 1] Ta-da.

08:42.689 --> 08:44.441
Is this from overseas?

08:44.524 --> 08:45.984
"Sang-yeong Park."

08:46.067 --> 08:49.029
Mr. Park sent it as a gift
before returning home.

08:49.112 --> 08:50.113
- [gasps]
- [employee 2] Ah.

08:50.196 --> 08:52.532
- Wow.
- He must be coming back soon.

08:53.408 --> 08:55.285
I bet he'll be back next month.

08:55.368 --> 08:57.454
[employee 3] Look, they have our initials.

08:57.537 --> 08:58.413
TO MI-JEONG, FROM SY

08:58.496 --> 08:59.831
Oh my.

08:59.914 --> 09:01.750
He really knows how to pick the best gift.

09:01.833 --> 09:03.626
[intriguing music playing]

09:03.710 --> 09:05.545
- [employee 2] Goodness.
- [employee 3] Wow.

09:05.628 --> 09:06.963
Sang-yeong?

09:07.047 --> 09:09.799
[Mi-rae]
Mr. Park, why are you doing this?

09:09.883 --> 09:11.384
If you do this,

09:11.468 --> 09:13.094
I'll look like the problem.

09:13.178 --> 09:15.555
- If this is about before…
- [Sang-yeong] Ms. Yu.

09:15.638 --> 09:18.558
People are watching.
We should keep some boundaries.

09:18.641 --> 09:20.602
And we shouldn't meet in private anymore.

09:20.685 --> 09:22.353
[Ok-hui] Why is she keeping
the door closed?

09:22.437 --> 09:25.023
Mi-ji, why are you still in bed?
What about the farm?

09:25.106 --> 09:26.357
[Mi-rae] I quit.

09:26.441 --> 09:27.442
What?

09:28.693 --> 09:32.739
Hey, did you quit
because of what I said before?

09:33.281 --> 09:34.616
[Mi-rae] I just quit.

09:37.160 --> 09:38.870
Let me sleep a bit longer.

09:42.207 --> 09:44.876
Gyeong-gu's here with the delivery.
Aren't you coming out?

09:44.959 --> 09:46.002
Later.

09:49.422 --> 09:51.674
Ms. Kim, this ramyeon is on me.

09:51.758 --> 09:53.718
- [Ok-hui] Hey, Gyeong-gu.
- Yes?

09:55.178 --> 09:56.805
Is something up with her?

09:57.680 --> 09:59.599
- [whispers] What do you mean?
- Nothing.

10:00.100 --> 10:03.478
It's just that she's been down all day.
She even quit the farm.

10:03.561 --> 10:06.022
- She quit the strawberry farm?
- Yes.

10:06.106 --> 10:08.650
Wow, Mi-ji.

10:08.733 --> 10:10.485
You really are loyal.

10:10.568 --> 10:13.113
The strawberry farm guy and the jam?

10:13.196 --> 10:14.948
I knew it all meant nothing.

10:15.448 --> 10:17.200
You can be our assistant deputy manager.

10:19.244 --> 10:20.286
Mi-ji!

10:22.872 --> 10:23.873
What's with her?

10:23.957 --> 10:27.627
Why don't you take her out
for some fresh air or something?

10:29.003 --> 10:30.630
[Gyeong-gu] All right, I guess.

10:31.548 --> 10:33.842
Just let her be for a while.

10:33.925 --> 10:36.010
[rock music playing on radio]

10:36.094 --> 10:37.137
Man.

10:37.220 --> 10:38.221
[in English] Hi!

10:38.304 --> 10:39.973
[in Korean] What are you doing,

10:40.056 --> 10:42.142
- stacking all this out here?
- [music volume lowers]

10:42.225 --> 10:43.184
- Well…
- Yes?

10:43.268 --> 10:45.812
It's annoying going back and forth
to the storage area.

10:45.895 --> 10:48.690
You know that fine dining places
manage tasks down to the second, right?

10:48.773 --> 10:52.402
[Il-lam] You really find
creative ways to waste time.

10:52.485 --> 10:53.820
Hurry and put them inside.

10:53.903 --> 10:56.406
What if the typhoon floods the whole farm?

10:56.489 --> 10:57.866
It's freezing. What typhoon?

10:57.949 --> 11:00.451
What kind of farmer
doesn't check the weather?

11:01.077 --> 11:03.872
A big typhoon is hitting
the central region this weekend.

11:03.955 --> 11:05.665
You should check
if the embankment is okay,

11:05.748 --> 11:07.792
otherwise this whole road
might end up underwater.

11:07.876 --> 11:10.044
If it floods, it floods.

11:10.128 --> 11:11.546
[Il-lam] Don't talk nonsense.

11:11.629 --> 11:13.506
Do it while I'm here.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.551
We've got sand right here.

11:16.634 --> 11:20.680
Just tell Mi-ji
to bring some extra sacks on her way.

11:20.763 --> 11:22.015
She quit.

11:22.098 --> 11:25.476
Quit… Mi-ji quit? Why?

11:27.145 --> 11:28.021
[exhales]

11:28.104 --> 11:30.481
Knowing you, I wondered
how she lasted that long.

11:30.565 --> 11:32.025
Then go get the sacks yourself

11:32.108 --> 11:34.277
- before I change my mind.
- [Se-jin] It's fine.

11:34.360 --> 11:37.113
We're the only farm on this side
of the river, so it doesn't matter.

11:37.197 --> 11:39.073
Will you swim out of here when it floods?

11:39.157 --> 11:42.035
If the bridge breaks,
you're stranded here, genius.

11:42.118 --> 11:44.787
So what? Did the bridge
kill my grandfather?

11:45.830 --> 11:47.040
[music volume rises]

11:48.750 --> 11:51.669
[Il-lam] So you're not fixing
the embankment today?

11:51.753 --> 11:53.755
[birds chirping]

11:58.134 --> 11:59.385
[quirky pensive music playing]

11:59.469 --> 12:02.180
SOBER UP!
SPARKLING GRAPEFRUIT

12:03.139 --> 12:04.891
[Mi-ji] Just say it.

12:04.974 --> 12:07.852
Who do you like right now?

12:08.728 --> 12:09.812
I also…

12:10.813 --> 12:11.981
Yes?

12:13.149 --> 12:14.901
I also want to say it.

12:14.984 --> 12:18.404
But not now. Not when you're like this.

12:18.488 --> 12:21.449
- What?
- Wait.

12:21.532 --> 12:23.826
Let's talk when you sober up.

12:23.910 --> 12:24.953
What?

12:27.163 --> 12:29.999
- [music fades]
- [heartbeat thumping]

12:31.417 --> 12:33.836
[tender music plays]

12:42.971 --> 12:44.055
[Ho-su grunts]

12:44.639 --> 12:46.099
[music fades]

12:49.185 --> 12:50.186
[sighs]

12:52.605 --> 12:53.773
[exhales]

12:56.317 --> 12:57.944
Why did I close my eyes?

13:02.782 --> 13:04.617
[cell phone buzzing]

13:07.745 --> 13:08.997
PARK JI-YUN

13:11.124 --> 13:12.417
Hey, Ji-yun.

13:14.961 --> 13:17.005
What? Slow down.

13:17.588 --> 13:19.090
[soft pop music playing over speakers]

13:19.173 --> 13:20.425
[camera shutter clicks]

13:22.844 --> 13:24.804
- [camera beeps]
- [camera shutter clicks]

13:25.847 --> 13:28.308
Didn't you say
it was urgent and important?

13:28.391 --> 13:30.393
It is urgent and important.

13:30.476 --> 13:32.478
I can't take photos
and do everything myself.

13:32.562 --> 13:34.772
- You could've come with someone else.
- Hey.

13:35.440 --> 13:37.108
Focus. You might break the heart.

13:40.236 --> 13:41.362
You're right.

13:41.446 --> 13:43.072
It didn't have to be you.

13:43.781 --> 13:45.575
But I told you last time

13:45.658 --> 13:47.744
that I'd make sure
you have a good time.

13:49.537 --> 13:52.665
This shot came out great.
Do you want to see it?

13:56.919 --> 13:58.796
I guess you really like this job.

13:58.880 --> 13:59.881
Me?

14:00.923 --> 14:02.300
That was random. Why?

14:02.383 --> 14:05.261
It just seems like you enjoy it.

14:06.137 --> 14:10.058
Well, I do like
new and interesting things.

14:10.600 --> 14:12.477
The job itself isn't bad.

14:13.102 --> 14:15.271
But it feels like
it's just about chasing trends.

14:15.355 --> 14:18.900
I'm thinking about moving somewhere
with more long-term potential.

14:23.571 --> 14:25.823
- Are you free tomorrow?
- I have plans in the afternoon.

14:25.907 --> 14:27.825
Then let's grab lunch before that.

14:27.909 --> 14:29.118
Sorry.

14:29.911 --> 14:32.497
I just realized I have something
in the morning too.

14:34.248 --> 14:36.084
Come on. Have lunch with me.

14:36.167 --> 14:39.712
The place I want to go to
only takes reservations for two or more.

14:39.796 --> 14:41.506
Go with your coworkers.

14:42.173 --> 14:43.966
I don't even know much about food.

14:44.592 --> 14:46.636
It's awkward with people from work.

14:47.678 --> 14:48.721
Please?

14:51.808 --> 14:52.809
[sighs]

14:53.559 --> 14:54.769
Just lunch, then.

14:55.686 --> 14:57.647
I really do have plans in the afternoon.

14:57.730 --> 14:58.940
Hey, Ho-su.

15:00.274 --> 15:01.567
What?

15:01.651 --> 15:03.528
You're surprisingly easy to convince.

15:04.278 --> 15:06.614
- That's not--
- Whatever. No take-backs.

15:07.156 --> 15:08.658
We're meeting tomorrow, okay?

15:10.910 --> 15:11.869
[sighs]

15:13.996 --> 15:15.373
[cell phone buzzes]

15:16.374 --> 15:19.085
[Ho-su] I've got your bag.
I'll come by your office.

15:19.168 --> 15:21.379
[Mi-ji] Just say it.

15:21.462 --> 15:23.047
- I also…
- [soft quirky music playing]

15:23.131 --> 15:26.926
I've already sorted things out,
so you don't need to worry.

15:27.009 --> 15:31.597
What on earth could've happened
for him to say it's all sorted?

15:32.515 --> 15:34.183
[groans]

15:34.267 --> 15:37.186
What did I do last night?

15:37.270 --> 15:38.729
[music concludes]

15:38.813 --> 15:41.399
Come on, brain. Give me something!

15:43.317 --> 15:44.986
- [Ji-yun] Mi-rae!
- [gasps softly]

15:45.570 --> 15:46.612
[Mi-ji] Oh…

15:47.363 --> 15:50.366
How come you two came together?

15:50.450 --> 15:52.118
We were nearby--

15:52.201 --> 15:55.246
We had dinner together,
and I tagged along to see you.

15:55.329 --> 15:56.789
Here's your bag.

15:57.415 --> 15:58.291
Right.

15:58.374 --> 15:59.459
[in English] Thank you.

16:00.751 --> 16:03.754
[sighs, in Korean]
Being here brings back memories.

16:05.047 --> 16:07.425
You don't need to borrow
my shoes today, right?

16:07.508 --> 16:08.509
What shoes?

16:09.510 --> 16:10.511
Interview day, remember?

16:12.346 --> 16:14.223
Don't act like you don't know.

16:14.932 --> 16:17.727
Ah, the shoes. Right.

16:17.810 --> 16:21.355
Why is there always a line at that place?

16:21.439 --> 16:22.815
AEWOL CROQUETTE

16:22.899 --> 16:25.568
That place was only on Jeju.
I guess they opened one here.

16:25.651 --> 16:26.819
Want to check it out?

16:26.903 --> 16:27.904
Now?

16:27.987 --> 16:29.864
Weren't you going back to work?

16:29.947 --> 16:31.866
[Ji-yun] It'll just be a quick stop.

16:31.949 --> 16:33.951
Mi-rae, we'll get going.

16:34.035 --> 16:35.703
- [Mi-ji] Okay.
- [Ji-yun] Let's go.

16:38.498 --> 16:40.750
You're coming
to the hospital tomorrow, right?

16:41.292 --> 16:42.251
[Mi-ji] Yes.

16:42.752 --> 16:43.961
See you there.

16:44.045 --> 16:45.296
All right. Bye.

16:50.718 --> 16:52.261
What the heck, Ho-su?

16:53.095 --> 16:55.348
Did you sort things out because of her?

16:59.685 --> 17:02.104
HIGH-QUALITY STRAWBERRY
GROWING GUIDE DRAFT

17:05.983 --> 17:07.652
DAILY FARM LOG

17:09.028 --> 17:10.404
EMPTY TRASH

17:10.488 --> 17:13.032
[gentle music playing]

17:13.115 --> 17:16.035
No. I can't let you go like this.

17:18.621 --> 17:20.122
I should at least know why.

17:21.791 --> 17:24.293
Don't dodge it with something vague
like "it's my problem."

17:24.377 --> 17:25.878
Let me know what's wrong!

17:25.962 --> 17:27.547
There are rumors.

17:29.757 --> 17:31.968
People are getting
the wrong idea about us.

17:32.927 --> 17:34.804
That's ridiculous…

17:36.013 --> 17:38.474
Are you seriously quitting
because of that?

17:38.558 --> 17:41.227
Because of stupid rumors
people are spreading for fun?

17:42.311 --> 17:43.396
[sighs]

17:43.938 --> 17:45.439
You can just deny it.

17:45.523 --> 17:47.817
Wouldn't it look weirder
to quit over some rumors?

17:48.568 --> 17:50.945
I'm getting rid of the reason
for the gossip.

17:51.028 --> 17:52.738
People who get swayed by gossip

17:53.489 --> 17:55.449
don't care about the truth anyway.

17:56.784 --> 17:59.203
You're the one getting swayed
the most right now.

18:00.538 --> 18:02.290
Those rumors are fake.

18:02.915 --> 18:05.793
But those strawberries are real.

18:05.876 --> 18:09.213
You're saying something fake
is more important than something real.

18:10.798 --> 18:11.799
Fine.

18:12.466 --> 18:14.385
Thank you for everything.

18:14.468 --> 18:15.553
Take care.

18:20.433 --> 18:21.559
[gentle music continues]

18:21.642 --> 18:22.768
[sighs]

18:22.852 --> 18:24.854
[cell phone buzzing]

18:30.610 --> 18:32.653
- Hey.
- [Mi-ji] What are you doing?

18:32.737 --> 18:35.489
- [music fades]
- Nothing much. Everything okay?

18:35.573 --> 18:36.866
Just the usual.

18:37.408 --> 18:38.826
Same old stuff at work.

18:39.744 --> 18:43.039
How have you been, Mi-rae?

18:44.290 --> 18:46.626
You know, I realized

18:46.709 --> 18:50.421
I always talk about myself,
but I never ask how you're doing.

18:51.297 --> 18:53.758
What do you do besides visiting Grandma?

18:53.841 --> 18:54.842
I just…

18:55.968 --> 18:57.928
worked at the strawberry farm.

18:59.180 --> 19:01.223
That 200,000-won-a-day job?

19:01.307 --> 19:04.143
No way. You worked on a farm?

19:04.226 --> 19:05.394
How was it?

19:05.478 --> 19:09.190
It's helped me to eat and sleep better.

19:09.273 --> 19:11.817
- [soft music playing]
- And it stopped me from overthinking.

19:11.901 --> 19:13.110
[Mi-ji] That's good.

19:13.194 --> 19:16.822
Getting your body moving
helps clear your mind.

19:16.906 --> 19:18.532
Hang in there until I come down.

19:18.616 --> 19:20.201
I'll take over when I get back.

19:21.118 --> 19:23.496
- I quit.
- Why?

19:24.914 --> 19:28.459
I just started wondering what I was doing.

19:28.542 --> 19:30.753
You're over there
dealing with my problems,

19:31.295 --> 19:33.214
and I'm here running away from reality.

19:33.297 --> 19:35.508
[Mi-ji] So what if you are?

19:35.591 --> 19:37.301
It's not like I have it that bad.

19:37.385 --> 19:39.595
The impact is different for you and me.

19:39.679 --> 19:40.805
I'm fine.

19:41.889 --> 19:43.432
I've been feeling anxious.

19:43.974 --> 19:48.020
The fact that I'm worrying again
might mean I'm getting back to normal.

19:49.939 --> 19:51.273
As for me,

19:51.357 --> 19:54.235
I'm only here until you're okay.

19:54.860 --> 19:56.278
We can switch back anytime.

19:57.029 --> 19:58.948
But if you're only saying this

19:59.031 --> 20:00.908
because you're worried about me,

20:00.991 --> 20:02.576
I can manage a bit longer.

20:03.953 --> 20:06.163
But are you really okay?

20:08.165 --> 20:09.208
It's just,

20:09.291 --> 20:12.294
I don't think it matters where I am.

20:12.795 --> 20:14.004
I'm still the same.

20:14.505 --> 20:15.589
[Mi-ji inhales]

20:15.673 --> 20:19.844
You've been saying "just" a lot.
Something's fishy.

20:20.511 --> 20:23.889
Are you sure you're okay to come back?
What about the resignation letter?

20:25.099 --> 20:26.142
I'll write it.

20:27.268 --> 20:29.520
Actually, let's end this next week.

20:31.647 --> 20:34.150
What? Next week?

20:34.233 --> 20:35.901
You want to switch next week?

20:36.527 --> 20:39.196
Yes. I was thinking of going back
around then anyway.

20:39.905 --> 20:41.782
We can switch sooner if you want.

20:41.866 --> 20:45.161
No, it's fine. Let's do it next week.

20:46.245 --> 20:48.080
Okay. Get some rest.

20:49.123 --> 20:51.125
- [sighs]
- [music fades]

20:51.208 --> 20:52.626
Next week?

20:52.710 --> 20:56.005
- There's nothing I can do as Mi-rae.
- [upbeat pop music playing over speakers]

20:56.088 --> 20:57.590
[Mi-ji inhales deeply]

20:57.673 --> 20:59.216
As for Ho-su,

20:59.300 --> 21:02.970
I'll settle things for real
once I'm back to myself next week.

21:03.053 --> 21:04.430
Whatever happens, happens.

21:04.513 --> 21:06.348
[breathes deeply]

21:06.432 --> 21:10.519
First, I need to clean up the mess I made
before Mi-rae comes back.

21:10.603 --> 21:12.813
DELETE TEXTS, HAIR APPOINTMENT
TALK TO TAE-I

21:13.481 --> 21:15.900
[inhales deeply]
What do I do with this one?

21:15.983 --> 21:17.026
NEW HQ PROJECT

21:17.109 --> 21:20.279
She'll be so mad at me
for not staying put.

21:24.450 --> 21:27.119
[breathes deeply]

21:31.624 --> 21:32.792
What are you looking at?

21:32.875 --> 21:34.668
Oh, it's nothing.

21:35.795 --> 21:36.962
Wait.

21:37.046 --> 21:40.174
How come you're not eating
at the cafeteria today?

21:40.257 --> 21:41.884
[gasps] No way.

21:42.468 --> 21:45.179
You didn't follow me here, did you?

21:45.262 --> 21:46.472
[scoffs]

21:50.684 --> 21:51.894
[Mi-ji clears throat]

21:55.189 --> 21:57.316
Hey, Tae-i.

21:57.399 --> 22:00.486
The other day, you asked

22:00.569 --> 22:04.198
if I knew Mr. Park was in charge
of the new HQ project when I took it on.

22:04.698 --> 22:06.200
Why did you ask?

22:06.826 --> 22:09.620
I didn't mean to accuse you or anything.

22:09.703 --> 22:11.205
I was just worried.

22:11.705 --> 22:13.040
About what?

22:14.625 --> 22:17.878
I'm just curious what others think.

22:17.962 --> 22:20.214
I figured working with Mr. Park

22:20.297 --> 22:22.049
might be uncomfortable for you.

22:23.175 --> 22:25.678
But if you're okay with it,
then that's all that matters.

22:25.761 --> 22:28.472
No need to avoid him
just because it's awkward.

22:28.556 --> 22:30.057
So don't mind what I said.

22:31.517 --> 22:32.560
Okay.

22:33.727 --> 22:34.854
[exhales]

22:37.147 --> 22:38.566
[cell phone buzzes]

22:48.534 --> 22:50.411
Who are you texting
that's making you smile?

22:50.494 --> 22:51.495
[chuckles softly]

22:51.579 --> 22:53.998
Wait, are you seeing someone?

22:54.081 --> 22:55.374
It's not like that.

22:57.334 --> 23:00.796
It's the old classmate
from the triple blind date.

23:01.380 --> 23:03.841
The lawyer from Wongeun?
The silent, cool guy?

23:03.924 --> 23:05.676
- [chuckles softly]
- Oh!

23:06.594 --> 23:08.470
[employee 1] What should we eat?

23:08.554 --> 23:11.807
[employee 2] Is it true
they're not renewing Ji-yun's contract?

23:11.891 --> 23:14.643
[employee 3] The team leader said
they're doing open recruitment.

23:14.727 --> 23:16.896
[employee 2] That's kind of harsh.

23:16.979 --> 23:20.566
Still, thanks to us,
she landed a lawyer boyfriend.

23:20.649 --> 23:22.651
- Maybe that's a silver lining.
- [chuckles]

23:22.735 --> 23:25.487
Is she really seeing a lawyer? Wow.

23:25.571 --> 23:28.407
[gasps] Does he know she's on contract?

23:28.490 --> 23:30.200
[employee 1] He does, actually.

23:30.284 --> 23:32.244
We told him at the blind date,
before she arrived.

23:32.328 --> 23:34.330
- [elevator dings]
- [employee 1] The elevator's here.

23:34.413 --> 23:36.332
[pensive music playing]

23:40.961 --> 23:42.254
[music fades]

23:44.798 --> 23:46.550
Aren't you going to take a photo?

23:46.634 --> 23:47.968
Why did you come today?

23:49.011 --> 23:51.013
Because I asked you to?

23:51.096 --> 23:53.891
You said you felt awkward
coming with your coworkers.

23:54.725 --> 23:56.393
So was it out of pity?

23:58.354 --> 24:01.440
I thought I was teasing you,
but it was the other way around.

24:02.733 --> 24:04.443
- What do you mean?
- You knew.

24:05.110 --> 24:07.321
That I was on contract.

24:08.197 --> 24:10.032
I bet you were laughing on the inside.

24:10.115 --> 24:11.450
I didn't know you knew,

24:11.533 --> 24:14.787
and I was out here
acting like I was some big shot.

24:16.121 --> 24:17.456
Does that matter?

24:20.501 --> 24:21.752
I knew you'd say that.

24:23.087 --> 24:25.005
It probably doesn't seem important to you.

24:26.423 --> 24:29.969
You don't care what other people think,
because you don't have to.

24:30.803 --> 24:33.764
Maybe it's because
I'm not as successful as you,

24:34.390 --> 24:36.517
but I can't ignore what others think.

24:36.600 --> 24:39.228
Since no one really sees me for who I am,

24:39.311 --> 24:41.563
I just go along
with what people want to see.

24:41.647 --> 24:42.940
That's why I didn't mention it.

24:43.023 --> 24:46.860
If anyone knew I was on contract,
would they even care to look at me?

24:48.028 --> 24:49.697
You're unbelievable, though.

24:50.197 --> 24:52.408
If you knew, you should've just told me.

24:53.117 --> 24:55.577
[sighs]
Now I'm too embarrassed about lying

24:55.661 --> 24:57.121
to ask you to meet up again.

24:57.997 --> 25:00.749
I even boasted about
making sure you'd have a good time.

25:02.084 --> 25:03.085
[inhales]

25:03.168 --> 25:05.337
But at least you had fun
watching me, right?

25:11.427 --> 25:12.428
Look.

25:13.846 --> 25:17.057
I get what you're saying, but…

25:18.434 --> 25:20.394
I never thought you lied.

25:21.854 --> 25:24.606
I don't see why anyone
has to mention being on contract.

25:25.274 --> 25:27.693
You love your job and work hard.

25:28.444 --> 25:29.820
That's not a lie.

25:31.488 --> 25:33.824
And I don't ignore what others think.

25:35.743 --> 25:36.744
I'm just awkward.

25:37.870 --> 25:39.038
[gentle music playing]

25:39.121 --> 25:42.082
It's not a choice.
I can't do things like you do.

25:42.166 --> 25:44.585
That's why I didn't realize
how you would feel.

25:47.337 --> 25:51.008
I didn't think you'd feel deceived
just because I didn't say anything.

25:52.301 --> 25:53.927
If I hurt your feelings,

25:54.553 --> 25:55.512
I'm sorry.

25:55.596 --> 25:56.972
[chuckles softly]

25:57.056 --> 25:58.390
What are you, a fool?

25:58.474 --> 26:00.768
Why are you apologizing? [chuckles]

26:01.685 --> 26:04.146
The more I get to know you,
the stranger you seem.

26:07.900 --> 26:09.068
Hey.

26:09.151 --> 26:10.819
Photo first!

26:13.197 --> 26:14.490
[giggles]

26:16.742 --> 26:18.327
[music fades]

26:18.410 --> 26:21.663
Did Mi-ji say anything to you?

26:23.040 --> 26:24.124
[Wol-sun] What?

26:25.959 --> 26:27.044
About what?

26:28.921 --> 26:29.922
Anything.

26:30.881 --> 26:32.674
She's been acting strange lately.

26:32.758 --> 26:35.260
What if she stays holed up
in her room again?

26:35.344 --> 26:37.262
[breathes deeply]

26:38.931 --> 26:41.016
Ask her to come and see you.
Say you miss her.

26:41.100 --> 26:42.768
She won't say no to you.

26:44.812 --> 26:45.979
Mi-ji…

26:47.940 --> 26:49.191
wouldn't do that.

26:49.274 --> 26:51.193
- [pensive music playing]
- Gosh.

26:52.152 --> 26:53.779
How do you know?

26:55.280 --> 26:57.741
What if giving her space
only makes her worse?

26:59.743 --> 27:01.870
She promised me.

27:02.913 --> 27:05.332
Mi-ji won't do that anymore.

27:06.834 --> 27:08.961
- [softly] She won't.
- Gosh.

27:09.670 --> 27:11.755
We can never see eye to eye.

27:12.422 --> 27:14.466
The owner of Rosa Restaurant
is hospitalized,

27:14.550 --> 27:18.345
so we're waiting for her to recover
before scheduling another meeting.

27:18.428 --> 27:20.889
If possible, I'd like to
speak with the owner alone.

27:20.973 --> 27:23.851
[inhales deeply] That might be difficult.

27:23.934 --> 27:25.769
She barely agreed to have a meeting.

27:27.229 --> 27:29.106
Who's in charge of Rosa Restaurant?

27:30.482 --> 27:31.775
That'd be me.

27:31.859 --> 27:33.068
[Chung-gu] Come on.

27:33.152 --> 27:34.903
You didn't convince her.

27:35.696 --> 27:36.655
Who's doing the work?

27:36.738 --> 27:37.865
Ah.

27:38.657 --> 27:41.201
She'll be off the project soon.

27:41.285 --> 27:42.369
Why?

27:42.452 --> 27:45.497
The previous person in charge
is coming back from overseas training.

27:45.581 --> 27:49.001
And those two are not on good terms.

27:50.711 --> 27:53.046
I'd like to meet the employee privately.

27:54.631 --> 27:55.841
Right now.

27:59.761 --> 28:00.721
[door opens]

28:05.100 --> 28:07.060
[intriguing music playing]

28:07.686 --> 28:12.232
How did you know
the whistleblower was my classmate?

28:12.858 --> 28:13.901
[chuckles]

28:17.613 --> 28:18.906
Sorry to bother you.

28:18.989 --> 28:22.201
I'm Lee Chung-gu, the attorney
helping with the Rosa Restaurant case.

28:22.284 --> 28:25.913
Hello, I'm Yu Mi-rae
from the Planning Strategy Team.

28:26.538 --> 28:29.625
You must have met
Ms. Kim Ro-sa several times.

28:29.708 --> 28:31.126
Have you gotten close?

28:31.919 --> 28:35.631
I've seen her a lot, so yes,
compared to when I first met her.

28:35.714 --> 28:37.216
How about Mr. Lee Ho-su?

28:37.799 --> 28:40.677
Since he's her representative,
I'd imagine you'd see him even more.

28:40.761 --> 28:43.555
- [music fades]
- If you're asking if we've gotten close,

28:43.639 --> 28:46.558
we already knew each other
from high school.

28:46.642 --> 28:48.352
Really? Was it a coincidence?

28:49.353 --> 28:52.439
- Or did you introduce them?
- No. [chuckles]

28:52.522 --> 28:55.150
Why would I go out of my way
to make things complicated?

28:55.234 --> 28:56.818
They had their own ties.

28:58.820 --> 28:59.988
I see.

29:00.072 --> 29:02.324
You seem honest.
I feel like I can trust you.

29:03.533 --> 29:04.576
[chuckles softly]

29:05.535 --> 29:08.247
About the new HQ project,
I heard you might step down

29:08.330 --> 29:09.706
over some tension with someone.

29:09.790 --> 29:13.794
If I took him out of the picture,
would you take the lead?

29:15.629 --> 29:17.881
What do you mean?

29:17.965 --> 29:19.424
Relax. Speak your mind.

29:19.508 --> 29:22.094
I don't really know anything
about the office politics here.

29:22.177 --> 29:23.971
All I need is to acquire the restaurant,

29:24.054 --> 29:27.933
and I think you're
the perfect fit for this job.

29:28.684 --> 29:30.310
[tense music playing]

29:34.606 --> 29:36.400
CONFIDENTIAL

29:36.608 --> 29:38.652
NEW HQ AND LRT LINE INTEGRATION PROJECT

29:39.861 --> 29:41.822
[page rustling]

29:44.616 --> 29:47.244
They're building an LRT station
at the new HQ site?

29:47.327 --> 29:49.246
Yes, you'll see the details there.

29:49.329 --> 29:51.456
The location of Rosa Restaurant
is crucial.

29:51.540 --> 29:53.250
Very few people know about this.

29:53.333 --> 29:56.086
If this information gets out,
things could get messy.

29:56.920 --> 29:58.588
Then why are you telling me…

29:58.672 --> 30:00.257
Because you're in charge.

30:00.340 --> 30:02.718
You should know the gravity of your work.

30:02.801 --> 30:05.429
Obviously, this is confidential.

30:05.512 --> 30:08.181
You can't tell anyone.
Not the owner, not your team,

30:08.265 --> 30:09.808
and not your family.

30:12.102 --> 30:14.688
And not your old classmate
you ran into by chance.

30:16.690 --> 30:17.816
[exhales]

30:19.735 --> 30:21.486
CONFIDENTIAL

30:22.237 --> 30:23.572
[music fades]

30:23.655 --> 30:24.656
[sighs]

30:24.740 --> 30:26.783
SEOUL SAEWON MEDICAL CENTER

30:28.910 --> 30:30.120
[Ro-sa] He's not here yet?

30:31.204 --> 30:32.664
Tell him we'll go on our own.

30:32.748 --> 30:35.000
He said he already left.

30:35.709 --> 30:38.003
Why is Ho-su taking so long?

30:39.546 --> 30:42.716
I was only in the hospital
for a few days, and look at all this.

30:42.799 --> 30:44.843
- Let me carry one.
- No way.

30:44.926 --> 30:46.970
Come on. Stop fussing over me.

30:47.054 --> 30:48.764
Seriously, no.

30:48.847 --> 30:49.931
[Ro-sa grumbles softly]

30:50.015 --> 30:51.683
You still need to be careful.

30:51.767 --> 30:52.934
[Ro-sa] Gosh.

30:56.605 --> 30:57.981
And…

30:58.065 --> 31:00.776
things have been hectic lately,

31:01.276 --> 31:03.779
so I didn't get a chance to say this.

31:03.862 --> 31:05.113
Thank you.

31:05.197 --> 31:06.073
Pardon?

31:06.948 --> 31:08.825
[loudly] I said, "Thank you."

31:11.912 --> 31:15.082
When I threw out my back that day,

31:15.832 --> 31:19.711
I figured I'd have the worst luck

31:19.795 --> 31:21.880
and starve to death lying there.

31:22.589 --> 31:24.257
No one was going to check on me,

31:24.841 --> 31:27.094
so I thought about
biting my tongue to end it.

31:27.677 --> 31:29.513
Then you showed up.

31:31.181 --> 31:34.601
If I'd known,
I wouldn't have been so mean to you.

31:35.811 --> 31:37.938
But how could I have known?

31:40.148 --> 31:43.193
Anyway, you saved me.

31:44.152 --> 31:45.237
Thank you.

31:46.738 --> 31:48.365
There's no need to thank me.

31:50.200 --> 31:51.785
I'm sorry.

31:53.245 --> 31:56.289
[chuckles] Sorry for what?

31:57.457 --> 31:58.542
Well…

32:00.293 --> 32:02.879
I mean… Actually…

32:06.049 --> 32:07.467
Sorry we're late.

32:08.343 --> 32:09.511
Ms. Ro-sa, please get in.

32:09.594 --> 32:11.221
Hello, ma'am.

32:11.304 --> 32:13.765
- [soft pensive music playing]
- [Ji-yun] Hey, Mi-rae.

32:14.349 --> 32:15.475
Hey.

32:17.811 --> 32:21.481
Why did you bring Ji-yun? It's awkward.

32:21.565 --> 32:24.317
She offered to give
your great-aunt a ride. I couldn't say no.

32:24.401 --> 32:26.987
How did you even…

32:27.070 --> 32:28.155
[door opens]

32:28.238 --> 32:30.365
- [whispers] Quiet.
- [music fades]

32:31.700 --> 32:33.743
What are you two whispering about?

32:33.827 --> 32:35.203
We were talking

32:35.287 --> 32:38.832
about where to put this
so it's easy to read.

32:39.374 --> 32:41.918
Should I leave it here?
No, it's better to stick it up here.

32:42.002 --> 32:43.420
POST-CHOLECYSTECTOMY PRECAUTIONS

32:43.753 --> 32:44.796
Oh!

32:45.338 --> 32:47.841
Is this you when you were young?

32:47.924 --> 32:51.761
Oh, you still look like your old self.

32:52.429 --> 32:55.849
Of course I do.
I may have aged, but I'm still me.

32:55.932 --> 32:59.186
Hmm. "Ro-sa and Sang-wol."

32:59.269 --> 33:00.645
Oh!

33:00.729 --> 33:05.317
So the "Sang-wol" in "The Sea of Sang-wol"
was a person?

33:06.359 --> 33:08.862
Wait. Is she Sang-wol?

33:09.488 --> 33:11.990
Is it okay to leave your friend alone?

33:12.073 --> 33:15.118
- Shouldn't you go downstairs?
- I'll go check on her.

33:15.202 --> 33:16.536
No, don't.

33:16.620 --> 33:19.247
Let me. I'll go.

33:19.331 --> 33:20.957
You can put this up.

33:21.500 --> 33:22.876
I don't mind going.

33:23.877 --> 33:24.878
[door opens]

33:28.340 --> 33:29.508
[camera shutter clicks]

33:31.343 --> 33:34.012
- [camera shutter clicks]
- Why are you taking so many pictures?

33:34.095 --> 33:35.263
Because I love it here.

33:35.347 --> 33:38.475
I've only seen retro-themed places,
but this place is real.

33:38.558 --> 33:39.726
Where's Ho-su?

33:39.809 --> 33:41.853
Upstairs. He'll be down soon.

33:43.355 --> 33:44.648
You've been seeing him a lot.

33:46.316 --> 33:48.193
What? Does it bother you?

33:49.236 --> 33:51.238
No, I'm just saying you see him a lot.

33:57.494 --> 33:58.954
What do you think of Ho-su?

34:01.540 --> 34:04.125
Ho-su is just Ho-su. What do you mean?

34:04.209 --> 34:05.877
Are you interested in him?

34:08.296 --> 34:10.799
I want to give it a shot with him.

34:10.882 --> 34:12.342
I wanted to check with you.

34:12.926 --> 34:15.345
[soft pensive music playing]

34:15.428 --> 34:18.682
[sighs] Do whatever you want.
Why do you care what I think?

34:18.765 --> 34:21.184
You know,
we always wanted the same things.

34:21.268 --> 34:22.686
College, jobs…

34:23.478 --> 34:25.230
You always got

34:25.730 --> 34:27.566
everything I desperately wished for.

34:29.234 --> 34:31.695
I tried everything to get into KFMC,

34:31.778 --> 34:35.240
but you got in half-heartedly
after quitting the civil service exam.

34:35.323 --> 34:38.660
Would you have applied there
if I hadn't pushed you to?

34:39.244 --> 34:40.370
Honestly?

34:42.914 --> 34:44.165
You're right.

34:44.916 --> 34:49.629
Anyway, you're doing well now,
so it all worked out.

34:50.255 --> 34:51.339
I'm on contract.

34:52.257 --> 34:54.426
It's about to end,
so I'll be unemployed soon.

34:54.509 --> 34:55.594
[chuckles]

34:56.219 --> 34:57.887
And for some reason,

34:57.971 --> 35:00.265
I just didn't want to tell you, Mi-rae.

35:01.224 --> 35:04.477
I wanted to pretend
I was doing just as well.

35:05.020 --> 35:06.730
It's all just insecurity, I guess.

35:08.523 --> 35:11.151
So this time, I'm calling dibs.

35:11.234 --> 35:12.777
I don't want to lose Ho-su too.

35:16.698 --> 35:19.618
Why do you like Ho-su?

35:21.411 --> 35:24.581
At first, he got my attention
because he's a lawyer.

35:25.915 --> 35:27.167
But I don't know…

35:27.876 --> 35:30.003
He seems so cold and indifferent,

35:30.879 --> 35:33.840
but he's actually gentle,
tender-hearted, awkward,

35:35.258 --> 35:36.968
and surprisingly…

35:38.511 --> 35:39.888
kind of…

35:42.891 --> 35:44.184
Foolish, right?

35:44.267 --> 35:46.186
[Ji-yun chuckling] Yes, he is.

35:46.895 --> 35:48.521
He's way too soft.

35:51.024 --> 35:52.734
He's so mysterious.

35:54.235 --> 35:56.571
That makes me want
to get to know him better.

35:57.572 --> 35:59.783
And see what's going on inside him.

36:01.701 --> 36:02.661
What?

36:03.203 --> 36:04.621
Do I sound childish?

36:05.955 --> 36:08.208
No. It sounds very mature.

36:08.291 --> 36:10.543
[Ji-yun chuckles] What?
Are you teasing me?

36:12.128 --> 36:13.129
No.

36:15.298 --> 36:16.508
I mean it.

36:17.217 --> 36:19.552
I like how honest you are.

36:23.598 --> 36:25.517
[Mi-ji] That being said…

36:28.353 --> 36:29.354
[music fades]

36:29.437 --> 36:30.730
You two go ahead.

36:31.314 --> 36:33.233
I have to stop by somewhere.

36:33.775 --> 36:35.026
Okay, Mi-rae.

36:35.860 --> 36:37.278
Stay on the main roads.

36:38.947 --> 36:40.240
Ho-su.

36:41.366 --> 36:42.450
[Ho-su] Okay.

36:45.036 --> 36:47.706
[soft pensive music playing]

36:50.083 --> 36:52.085
[Mi-ji] What is this feeling?

36:52.168 --> 36:54.546
It's like I've lost
before the fight began.

37:02.345 --> 37:04.222
We spent ten years out of sync.

37:04.305 --> 37:06.307
Is our timing off again?

37:07.183 --> 37:09.477
[sighs] I just need one more week.

37:10.061 --> 37:12.605
I never really
got to talk to him as myself.

37:15.817 --> 37:17.861
But even if I go back to being me,

37:17.944 --> 37:19.654
do I have a chance?

37:21.448 --> 37:23.700
First loves belong in the past,

37:24.200 --> 37:26.745
and I have nothing to be proud of.

37:31.583 --> 37:33.209
It's just sad.

37:33.835 --> 37:35.795
My feelings always go to waste

37:36.504 --> 37:39.299
before they're ever heard.

37:47.015 --> 37:48.516
[music concludes]

37:48.600 --> 37:52.395
What do you mean
you want me to counsel Mi-ji?

37:52.479 --> 37:53.897
That's nonsense.

37:54.689 --> 37:56.024
Why not?

37:56.900 --> 37:58.568
Don't you have a counseling certificate?

37:58.651 --> 38:01.696
That's for kids. Mi-ji is…

38:01.780 --> 38:04.699
Besides, young people these days
don't like people interfering.

38:04.783 --> 38:07.202
Mi-ji is still a child inside.

38:07.285 --> 38:10.538
Just think of her as a fifth grader
and talk to her, will you?

38:10.622 --> 38:12.415
If you're so worried,
talk to her yourself.

38:12.499 --> 38:15.418
I'm asking because I can't!

38:15.502 --> 38:17.462
Why not?

38:17.545 --> 38:19.047
You're her mom.

38:19.130 --> 38:20.799
Some moms aren't as good as others.

38:24.844 --> 38:27.472
What kind of mom
can't tell her own kids apart?

38:29.474 --> 38:30.600
Come on.

38:31.267 --> 38:34.270
Mi-ji and Mi-rae look exactly alike.

38:34.354 --> 38:36.231
Anyone would be confused.

38:37.190 --> 38:38.441
But I'm their mom.

38:40.860 --> 38:43.780
I spent all their childhood working,
barely paying attention to them.

38:43.863 --> 38:46.074
Trying to act like a mom now won't work.

38:46.908 --> 38:49.494
After their dad died
and their grandma collapsed…

38:51.329 --> 38:54.249
Mi-ji doesn't have anyone
she can really open up to.

38:57.210 --> 39:00.588
Just let her know how much you care.

39:00.672 --> 39:03.716
- Then it should be fine.
- I don't know.

39:04.259 --> 39:06.594
I just can't do that with Mi-ji.

39:09.222 --> 39:12.809
She reminds me so much of myself,
and I always say the wrong thing.

39:16.104 --> 39:18.356
How long has Mi-ji been in her room for?

39:18.898 --> 39:20.024
[whispers] Three days.

39:21.526 --> 39:22.986
[laughs]

39:23.069 --> 39:24.529
Are you kidding me?

39:24.612 --> 39:25.780
Ok-hui!

39:25.864 --> 39:28.533
I don't leave my room
for five days during the break.

39:28.616 --> 39:31.911
You're so dramatic
for someone who doesn't care.

39:31.995 --> 39:34.289
- Bun-hong.
- Get out of the way.

39:34.372 --> 39:38.668
I'm not being dramatic.
I'm seriously worried!

39:38.751 --> 39:42.130
Talk to me again
if she stays in there for a month.

39:42.213 --> 39:44.507
And stop humble-bragging
about having daughters.

39:44.591 --> 39:46.676
I'm swamped as it is… [clicks tongue]

39:46.759 --> 39:49.095
- [paper rustling]
- [Bun-hong] Are we done?

39:49.178 --> 39:51.222
[soft pensive music playing]

39:52.140 --> 39:55.268
[grunting]

40:01.399 --> 40:02.400
No!

40:07.697 --> 40:08.740
[sighs]

40:20.585 --> 40:23.421
- [music fades]
- [Se-jin] Please throw this junk away.

40:23.504 --> 40:26.174
I bought you that expensive chair
so you could get rid of this junk.

40:26.257 --> 40:27.550
And those clothes!

40:27.634 --> 40:30.345
So you ditched the Gore-Tex vest
and went back to that rag again?

40:30.428 --> 40:31.554
Toss it already.

40:31.638 --> 40:34.474
It doesn't have any holes.
How is it a rag?

40:34.557 --> 40:37.018
Why don't you throw out
those worn-out sneakers?

40:37.101 --> 40:39.771
These are intentionally distressed.

40:39.854 --> 40:43.066
Man, it's so shabby
that I can't bear to look at it.

40:43.149 --> 40:46.611
If you don't want to see it,
just go back to Seoul.

40:46.694 --> 40:50.490
Why do you keep coming down here?

40:51.032 --> 40:53.034
Just to throw away perfectly good stuff?

40:54.202 --> 40:55.453
You didn't know?

40:55.536 --> 40:59.958
My goal is to clear out everything you own
and replace it all with new stuff.

41:00.041 --> 41:03.086
Or you can move to Seoul with me.
Let's see who wins.

41:03.169 --> 41:06.381
- [birds chirping]
- [gentle music playing]

41:11.094 --> 41:14.764
[man] Wow.
This place is bigger than I thought.

41:15.264 --> 41:17.517
Your grandfather ran all this by himself?

41:17.600 --> 41:19.477
If it's too much to handle…

41:26.609 --> 41:27.986
[Se-jin sighs heavily]

41:31.280 --> 41:32.532
[inhales deeply]

41:33.282 --> 41:35.493
[sobs]

41:41.332 --> 41:42.917
[gentle music continues]

41:52.010 --> 41:53.177
[Se-jin sighs]

41:56.806 --> 41:58.683
[music fades]

42:01.102 --> 42:02.687
[sighs, mutters]

42:07.108 --> 42:08.609
Did you lose something?

42:08.693 --> 42:09.694
The LRT…

42:11.821 --> 42:13.031
Mm.

42:13.114 --> 42:15.950
I think I left something on the LRT.
[chuckles softly]

42:16.034 --> 42:17.243
You can go.

42:22.582 --> 42:23.624
[sighs]

42:23.708 --> 42:26.044
Where could it be? It's not at home.

42:26.836 --> 42:29.505
- Gosh, this is driving me crazy.
- [cell phone buzzing]

42:32.008 --> 42:33.259
Hey, Seung-hyeon.

42:34.886 --> 42:35.845
What?

42:36.345 --> 42:37.722
The wedding?

42:37.805 --> 42:39.015
Oh.

42:39.098 --> 42:41.350
- Is that this weekend?
- [Seung-hyeon] Yes.

42:41.851 --> 42:44.604
If you're going, let's go together.
I'll pick you up.

42:44.687 --> 42:48.024
[Mi-ji] I can just take the bus.

42:48.107 --> 42:51.194
[chuckles] You haven't seen
where it is, have you?

42:51.277 --> 42:55.114
The venue's up on a hill,
so you'll need a car to get there.

42:56.449 --> 42:59.285
Wait. Do you already have
someone to go with?

42:59.869 --> 43:02.246
I just thought you might be going alone

43:02.330 --> 43:04.415
since Ji-yun is going with Ho-su.

43:06.167 --> 43:08.711
Ho-su is going with Ji-yun?

43:08.795 --> 43:11.047
[Seung-hyeon] Yes, didn't he tell you?

43:11.130 --> 43:13.966
No. I didn't even know he was going.

43:14.050 --> 43:15.134
Really?

43:16.052 --> 43:18.930
Maybe they wanted
some alone time. [chuckles]

43:19.555 --> 43:23.351
If you're okay with it, I can pick you up.
I'm heading that way anyway.

43:23.434 --> 43:24.560
Uh…

43:25.186 --> 43:27.146
[vacuum whirring]

43:30.399 --> 43:31.609
[whirring stops]

43:47.667 --> 43:48.626
[door sliding open]

43:54.382 --> 43:55.591
[Mi-ji groans]

43:56.717 --> 43:59.220
[mumbling] It's so itchy.

44:01.139 --> 44:02.807
Why is this…

44:03.349 --> 44:04.934
It's too tight…

44:06.227 --> 44:08.062
Can you…

44:23.995 --> 44:25.121
[Mi-ji grunts softly]

44:44.348 --> 44:45.433
[grunts softly]

44:51.189 --> 44:53.733
[tender music playing]

44:53.816 --> 44:55.234
[heartbeat thumping faintly]

45:21.052 --> 45:23.346
[music fades]

45:24.555 --> 45:25.848
JI-YUN

45:28.184 --> 45:29.185
Jeez.

45:29.268 --> 45:30.937
[cell phone buzzing]

45:32.772 --> 45:33.814
[clears throat]

45:36.192 --> 45:37.526
Hey, what's up?

45:38.277 --> 45:40.029
[Ho-su] Didn't you lose something?

45:40.863 --> 45:42.073
What do you mean?

45:43.407 --> 45:47.245
[gasps] Do you have that LRT file?

45:47.328 --> 45:50.331
- [indistinct chatter]
- [soft pop music playing over speakers]

45:54.293 --> 45:55.503
Anything else?

45:57.046 --> 46:00.466
Why don't you just give me
your door code while you're at it?

46:00.549 --> 46:02.677
Door code? 36936--

46:02.760 --> 46:04.095
[Ho-su] No.

46:04.178 --> 46:06.472
Why are you telling me
something you're not supposed to?

46:06.555 --> 46:08.766
Have you told anyone else besides me?

46:08.849 --> 46:10.643
No, just you.

46:10.726 --> 46:13.729
If this gets out,
the lawyer said I could get sued.

46:13.813 --> 46:15.898
Not "could." You 100% would.

46:16.899 --> 46:20.194
If someone else heard this,
you'd be in serious trouble.

46:21.529 --> 46:23.155
I know.

46:24.365 --> 46:27.952
Shouldn't we tell Ms. Ro-sa about this?

46:28.035 --> 46:31.539
I can't ask her to sell the building
while hiding something so important.

46:31.622 --> 46:32.999
It's just wrong.

46:33.541 --> 46:35.876
You work for KFMC, not her.

46:36.377 --> 46:37.378
That's your job.

46:37.461 --> 46:40.548
I didn't know about it before,
but now I do.

46:41.215 --> 46:44.719
If I go through with it anyway,
it'd feel like I'm deceiving her.

46:44.802 --> 46:47.763
What if she sells
and then regrets it later?

46:50.891 --> 46:52.018
[sighs]

46:52.810 --> 46:55.521
I get how you feel.
But you need to drop it.

46:57.106 --> 46:59.358
You didn't say anything today,

46:59.442 --> 47:00.985
and I didn't hear a thing.

47:01.736 --> 47:04.488
But that doesn't make it go away…

47:04.572 --> 47:06.949
[Ho-su] Fine, then let's put it this way.

47:07.575 --> 47:10.369
You told me, but I chose not to tell her.

47:10.953 --> 47:14.332
But from this moment on, officially,

47:14.415 --> 47:16.834
you have said nothing. Got it?

47:17.501 --> 47:18.669
[sighs]

47:19.712 --> 47:20.921
Nothing.

47:23.174 --> 47:24.300
Fine.

47:29.388 --> 47:33.017
YU MI-RAE
SENIOR SPECIALIST

47:33.976 --> 47:35.436
[inhales]

47:37.855 --> 47:39.648
About the LRT station.

47:39.732 --> 47:40.858
Have you told anyone?

47:41.859 --> 47:44.528
[innocently] Me? Not at all.

47:44.612 --> 47:46.697
- [chuckles]
- Then why are you so nervous?

47:47.406 --> 47:48.783
We're on the same team.

47:48.866 --> 47:49.784
[exhales]

47:50.409 --> 47:52.036
We are, right?

47:53.746 --> 47:55.164
Of course.

47:55.790 --> 47:56.957
On the same team.

47:57.041 --> 47:58.501
[both chuckle softly]

47:59.210 --> 48:01.420
So, I think we should start negotiating.

48:01.504 --> 48:05.716
Can you set up a meeting next week
with Rosa Restaurant's representative?

48:05.800 --> 48:07.885
Sure. Next week it is.

48:07.968 --> 48:10.971
And there's something I wanted to ask you.

48:12.139 --> 48:15.351
It's hard to match faces
since it's an old photo.

48:15.434 --> 48:17.103
[tense music playing]

48:17.186 --> 48:18.813
[Chung-gu] From what I've heard…

48:19.605 --> 48:22.817
this is poet Kim Ro-sa. Is that right?

48:30.950 --> 48:33.661
[Mi-ji] Is this you when you were young?

48:33.744 --> 48:35.788
Wait, is she Sang-wol?

48:36.372 --> 48:37.915
SEPTEMBER 3, 1975

48:37.998 --> 48:40.501
What? That's not her?

48:41.293 --> 48:42.628
Jeez.

48:42.711 --> 48:44.922
The photo is too old. I can't tell.

48:46.465 --> 48:49.510
If that's Kim Ro-sa, the sociology major,
then it must be her.

48:49.593 --> 48:51.262
[photograph rustling]

48:51.345 --> 48:52.763
I was just checking.

48:52.847 --> 48:56.100
She looks so different
from her recent photos.

48:56.600 --> 48:58.936
[grunts softly] Well…

49:03.566 --> 49:04.608
[knife thudding]

49:04.692 --> 49:06.485
[music fades]

49:11.866 --> 49:15.786
[Mi-ji] That woman.
I swear that was Sang-wol.

49:16.370 --> 49:17.830
Did they have the same major?

49:18.330 --> 49:21.000
But he said she was Kim Ro-sa, the poet…

49:21.500 --> 49:23.377
[Ro-sa] Ho-su is running a bit late.

49:25.129 --> 49:28.215
- Have you finished writing?
- Yes, I'll put this up.

49:29.175 --> 49:30.301
This is yours, right?

49:32.845 --> 49:34.346
Uh… Uh…

49:35.222 --> 49:37.558
Did you take a look?

49:38.225 --> 49:40.144
I did. I was wondering what it was.

49:40.936 --> 49:42.897
I mean… [breathes heavily]

49:43.522 --> 49:44.648
It's confidential.

49:45.566 --> 49:47.735
Because of company policy…

49:47.818 --> 49:50.196
How can you be so careless
with something like that?

49:50.279 --> 49:51.322
Here.

49:52.239 --> 49:53.282
What?

49:54.325 --> 49:55.326
Is that…

49:56.452 --> 49:57.495
all?

49:57.578 --> 49:59.413
Aren't you going to say anything else?

49:59.497 --> 50:01.874
Take better care of your stuff.

50:04.585 --> 50:07.588
Did you write that we're closed
on weekends for now?

50:07.671 --> 50:09.215
What? Yes.

50:14.178 --> 50:16.263
CLOSED ON WEEKENDS
FOR THE TIME BEING

50:16.347 --> 50:18.557
[pensive music playing]

50:28.400 --> 50:30.319
[Ro-sa] I did.
I was wondering what it was.

50:30.402 --> 50:32.363
Did you write that we're closed
on weekends for now?

50:32.446 --> 50:34.073
I put a note on your door.

50:34.156 --> 50:35.616
- You didn't see it?
- What note?

50:35.699 --> 50:38.118
This is poet Kim Ro-sa. Is that right?

50:38.202 --> 50:39.745
[Mi-ji] Wait. Is she Sang-wol?

50:40.329 --> 50:41.664
[exhales]

50:42.706 --> 50:44.833
[Ho-su] What are you doing standing there?

50:48.587 --> 50:49.755
Ho-su.

50:50.297 --> 50:51.465
[music fades]

50:51.549 --> 50:53.092
Yes, I know.

50:53.175 --> 50:54.552
You know?

50:55.427 --> 50:57.346
So she can't read?

50:58.806 --> 51:01.308
It's not that she can't read at all.

51:01.392 --> 51:03.352
I think she has dyslexia.

51:03.435 --> 51:05.938
She can read and write
simple words, like names.

51:06.021 --> 51:07.356
How did you…

51:08.023 --> 51:09.650
When did you figure it out?

51:10.359 --> 51:11.694
I just noticed over time.

51:11.777 --> 51:14.488
That's probably why
she made me her representative.

51:15.197 --> 51:16.240
Why?

51:16.323 --> 51:17.241
[gasps]

51:17.324 --> 51:22.162
Is it even possible
to go to HNU if you can't read?

51:22.246 --> 51:24.665
There was someone like that
in my department too.

51:25.666 --> 51:27.668
Dyslexia isn't an illness.
It's a condition.

51:27.751 --> 51:29.712
It can definitely be improved.

51:29.795 --> 51:31.964
Maybe some people do get better,

51:32.047 --> 51:34.258
but she still can't read.

51:37.428 --> 51:39.388
So what are you trying to say?

51:39.471 --> 51:41.432
You think she faked her degree?

51:43.100 --> 51:44.768
How are you so calm?

51:44.852 --> 51:46.854
Doesn't this seem weird to you?

51:46.937 --> 51:48.147
It does.

51:48.731 --> 51:52.443
But so what? Are we supposed to dig up
her student records from 50 years ago?

51:52.526 --> 51:53.611
For what?

51:54.194 --> 51:56.530
It's not just about her degree.

51:57.072 --> 51:58.949
She's a poet.

51:59.908 --> 52:03.287
If she's hiding something…

52:03.370 --> 52:05.998
People always have a reason
for hiding things.

52:06.081 --> 52:08.125
And you need a reason to dig it up too.

52:09.084 --> 52:10.794
So we just pretend we don't know?

52:10.878 --> 52:14.340
Isn't it kind of shady to act that way?

52:15.507 --> 52:17.760
We don't know everything, do we?

52:19.553 --> 52:21.472
And if you don't know the full story,

52:22.514 --> 52:24.516
it's better to keep quiet sometimes.

52:25.225 --> 52:29.104
Are you telling me
to keep my mouth shut?

52:29.188 --> 52:32.399
We all have that one question
we don't want to be asked.

52:32.941 --> 52:36.862
Does choosing not to ask it
count as being deceitful?

52:38.530 --> 52:39.907
But still…

52:40.949 --> 52:43.452
Whatever. Let's just say
I'm the shady one.

52:44.453 --> 52:45.954
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

52:46.038 --> 52:48.332
- Bye.
- Hey, Ho-su.

52:49.124 --> 52:50.376
[card reader beeps]

52:53.921 --> 52:56.674
[Mi-ji] When did he figure all that out?

52:56.757 --> 52:59.176
[sighs] He's impossible to read.

53:01.679 --> 53:02.680
[sighs]

53:02.763 --> 53:05.307
[car horn continues honking]

53:05.391 --> 53:07.601
[engine rumbling]

53:07.685 --> 53:09.645
[car horn continues honking]

53:09.728 --> 53:11.271
What are you doing?

53:12.898 --> 53:15.275
Why weren't you answering your phone?

53:15.359 --> 53:17.820
I had to make a scene just to see you!

53:18.946 --> 53:20.114
Get in.

53:20.197 --> 53:21.490
Where are we going?

53:22.991 --> 53:24.159
Well,

53:24.243 --> 53:27.121
it's urgent, so just get in.
I'll explain on the way.

53:27.705 --> 53:30.416
We don't have time, okay? Hurry up.

53:31.250 --> 53:32.292
[Gyeong-gu grunts]

53:32.376 --> 53:34.253
- [car horn honking]
- Fine, I'm coming.

53:36.171 --> 53:38.215
- [car horn honking]
- I'm coming.

53:47.558 --> 53:49.476
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR WEDDING

53:49.560 --> 53:50.811
Traffic's pretty bad.

53:52.604 --> 53:54.857
It's nice to spend
more time with you, though.

53:57.025 --> 53:59.069
Dang, you really went all out today.

53:59.153 --> 54:00.654
Trying to outshine the bride?

54:00.738 --> 54:02.573
Oh, please.

54:03.615 --> 54:07.119
Anyway, thanks for the ride.

54:07.202 --> 54:09.455
[chuckles softly] No problem.

54:11.039 --> 54:12.416
By the way,

54:12.499 --> 54:14.835
I heard there will be
some familiar faces today.

54:14.918 --> 54:16.253
Did you get a heads-up?

54:17.755 --> 54:19.047
No. Who?

54:21.550 --> 54:23.552
I guess they're dropping by unannounced.

54:25.763 --> 54:28.265
A couple will make a surprise appearance.

54:31.351 --> 54:33.812
- [calm chatter]
- [soft piano music playing]

54:41.195 --> 54:42.237
[Seung-hyeon] How are you?

54:42.321 --> 54:44.490
- [classmate 1] Good.
- It's been a while. [chuckles]

54:44.573 --> 54:46.200
- [classmate 2] You're here!
- Hey.

54:48.786 --> 54:51.205
So that's why you wanted me
to save two seats.

54:51.288 --> 54:52.706
You were coming with Mi-rae.

54:53.832 --> 54:55.209
[Seung-hyeon in English] Thank you.

54:55.292 --> 54:57.753
[in Korean] Man,
the traffic was insane. Right?

54:58.754 --> 55:00.339
Oh? Ho-su, you made it.

55:00.964 --> 55:01.965
Yes.

55:04.510 --> 55:08.555
[chuckles] Ho-su, isn't that hilarious?

55:08.639 --> 55:09.932
Look at that.

55:10.015 --> 55:11.141
What? Oh.

55:11.642 --> 55:12.976
[Ji-yun] Over there.

55:13.060 --> 55:14.561
- Yes, it is.
- [Ji-yun chuckles]

55:17.231 --> 55:20.234
[sighs] Where are we even going?

55:20.818 --> 55:23.403
You'll see when we get there.

55:23.487 --> 55:26.406
Jeez, stop rushing me.

55:26.490 --> 55:28.158
We're almost there.

55:28.867 --> 55:31.328
You dragged me all the way
to Seoul while saying that.

55:31.411 --> 55:34.039
Why are you getting so worked up?

55:34.122 --> 55:36.959
Just take a look at the thing back there.

55:37.751 --> 55:38.877
[exhales]

55:42.881 --> 55:46.635
Seriously, where are we going?
And what's with this outfit?

55:46.718 --> 55:48.387
It's pretty, isn't it?

55:48.929 --> 55:52.057
What you're wearing is not appropriate.

55:53.058 --> 55:55.185
We're going to a wedding!

55:55.269 --> 55:56.478
Whose wedding?

55:56.562 --> 55:58.105
You know them.

55:58.188 --> 56:01.567
Their kid just turned one,
and they're finally holding the ceremony.

56:03.193 --> 56:04.736
Min-jae and Eun-su?

56:05.737 --> 56:07.573
You got an invitation too?

56:08.407 --> 56:09.908
[Gyeong-gu] Man, those two.

56:09.992 --> 56:12.494
If they invited you as well,

56:12.578 --> 56:15.205
they must be trying to cash in
on wedding gifts.

56:15.747 --> 56:18.083
Anyway, the wedding is just an excuse.

56:18.959 --> 56:22.254
Let's just have a cozy little date,
just you and me.

56:22.337 --> 56:24.214
- A date?
- Yes.

56:24.882 --> 56:28.760
You've been holed up lately,
digging around in your own world.

56:29.970 --> 56:32.806
Mi-ji, I know you were
shutting yourself in

56:32.890 --> 56:34.850
just to get some attention.

56:36.184 --> 56:39.062
This guy got you out for some fresh air,

56:39.146 --> 56:41.857
rented a car and booked a hotel.

56:42.524 --> 56:43.609
What? A hotel?

56:43.692 --> 56:45.944
We just got here.
We should stay overnight.

56:46.028 --> 56:47.696
Don't worry. I told your mom

56:47.779 --> 56:50.991
we're going to the wedding.
We've got a solid alibi.

56:51.074 --> 56:53.410
Have you heard
of the Sauron Tower in Jamsil?

56:53.493 --> 56:55.037
It's amazing.

56:55.120 --> 56:58.123
I even paid extra for a river view--

56:58.206 --> 56:59.291
Pull over.

57:00.250 --> 57:01.501
Why? We're almost there.

57:01.585 --> 57:03.629
I said pull over right now!

57:10.761 --> 57:13.805
[Gyeong-gu] Hey, Mi-ji!

57:15.766 --> 57:17.142
Hey!

57:17.225 --> 57:19.019
What's with you all of a sudden?

57:19.102 --> 57:20.687
No, what's with you?

57:20.771 --> 57:23.565
This is way out of line!

57:23.649 --> 57:25.025
What is?

57:25.651 --> 57:27.736
You basically kidnapped me in your car.

57:27.819 --> 57:29.821
And what? You booked a room?

57:29.905 --> 57:33.367
[chuckles] You know the kidnapping thing
was just an act.

57:33.450 --> 57:36.078
- That's our thing.
- What thing?

57:36.161 --> 57:39.498
Just because you're my ex,
I'm supposed to go along with whatever?

57:39.581 --> 57:40.666
Mi-ji, you…

57:40.749 --> 57:43.251
I tried to overlook it,
but I can't anymore.

57:43.335 --> 57:46.630
There are boundaries
between men and women.

57:46.713 --> 57:50.175
You really shouldn't cross the line
just because we're close!

57:53.887 --> 57:54.846
What's going on?

57:55.472 --> 57:56.431
What?

57:58.100 --> 57:59.851
[suspenseful music playing]

57:59.935 --> 58:01.144
Ah…

58:08.777 --> 58:10.237
You're not Mi-ji, are you?

58:10.320 --> 58:11.321
[music builds, concludes]

58:11.405 --> 58:12.781
- Hey, guys!
- [Min-jae chuckles]

58:12.864 --> 58:14.700
It feels like his birthday party,
not a wedding.

58:14.783 --> 58:16.743
I can't think straight
because of this kid.

58:16.827 --> 58:19.413
What are you talking about?
He's the star of the wedding, right?

58:19.496 --> 58:21.665
[Min-jae chuckles]
Thanks for coming, everyone.

58:21.748 --> 58:23.166
Let's all get together

58:23.250 --> 58:25.460
- for an after-party soon, okay?
- Sounds good.

58:25.544 --> 58:26.795
[Eun-su] Enjoy your food.

58:29.506 --> 58:31.049
The food here is great.

58:31.133 --> 58:32.718
Isn't this venue nice?

58:33.760 --> 58:35.262
Yes, it is.

58:36.138 --> 58:38.890
[Mi-ji] Are you two here
to check out the venue?

58:44.688 --> 58:46.273
[chuckles]

58:46.356 --> 58:48.066
Mi-rae, you're going hard today.

58:53.405 --> 58:55.490
Ho-su, do you want some too?

58:59.327 --> 59:01.079
[laughs]

59:01.872 --> 59:04.249
What's with you?
You're making him feel awkward.

59:06.001 --> 59:07.044
Don't mind him.

59:11.006 --> 59:12.174
[Seung-hyeon groans]

59:12.966 --> 59:16.386
He said he'd come, no matter how late,
but it looks like he's not coming.

59:16.470 --> 59:17.888
Why? Is someone coming?

59:17.971 --> 59:19.723
Yes, surprise guests.

59:20.807 --> 59:21.683
Gyeong-gu.

59:22.642 --> 59:25.187
[coughs] Song Gyeong-gu?

59:25.270 --> 59:27.522
Remember the couple I told you about?

59:27.606 --> 59:30.942
Gyeong-gu was supposed
to bring Mi-ji today.

59:32.110 --> 59:33.695
- Mi-ji?
- [Seung-hyeon chuckles]

59:33.779 --> 59:36.740
This could've actually been fun for once.
What a shame.

59:36.823 --> 59:38.366
Why would that be fun?

59:39.659 --> 59:41.328
I haven't seen them in so long.

59:41.411 --> 59:44.122
What's so fun about
seeing those two after so long?

59:45.415 --> 59:46.917
- [chuckles]
- [tense music playing]

59:47.000 --> 59:49.669
Don't be a buzzkill. I was just…

59:49.753 --> 59:53.006
Aren't you a bit old
to still find that crap fun?

59:53.090 --> 59:54.341
[scoffs]

59:57.010 --> 59:58.011
No.

59:58.553 --> 01:00:00.430
It's more fun now that I'm older.

01:00:02.974 --> 01:00:04.434
You've always been like this…

01:00:04.518 --> 01:00:05.644
What, you jerk?

01:00:05.727 --> 01:00:07.312
- You think I don't know?
- About what?

01:00:07.395 --> 01:00:09.022
Ho-su, what's your problem?

01:00:09.106 --> 01:00:10.774
- Stop, Ho-su.
- [Ji-yun] Knock it off.

01:00:10.857 --> 01:00:13.276
- [Seung-hyeon] A lawyer throwing punches?
- What's wrong?

01:00:13.360 --> 01:00:14.402
[Mi-ji] Come on.

01:00:16.488 --> 01:00:17.781
[Ho-su sighs]

01:00:18.365 --> 01:00:19.491
Ho-su, wait up.

01:00:19.574 --> 01:00:21.034
We'll get going.

01:00:21.118 --> 01:00:23.036
[Seung-hyeon scoffs] Jeez.

01:00:23.120 --> 01:00:24.913
[Mi-ji] What's with him?

01:00:24.996 --> 01:00:26.915
I've never seen Ho-su
act like that before.

01:00:26.998 --> 01:00:29.334
He's always been weird around me.

01:00:29.417 --> 01:00:31.628
Does he have anger issues or something?

01:00:33.338 --> 01:00:34.840
[music fades]

01:00:34.923 --> 01:00:37.050
Did something happen between you two?

01:00:38.343 --> 01:00:40.387
Back in the day… [clicks tongue]

01:00:40.470 --> 01:00:42.848
[chuckles] It's embarrassing
to even talk about.

01:00:44.141 --> 01:00:46.977
Remember Gyeong-gu's
big love confession in senior year?

01:00:47.060 --> 01:00:48.270
[Gyeong-gu] I like you.

01:00:49.104 --> 01:00:51.731
[pensive music playing]

01:00:55.360 --> 01:00:57.279
[music builds]

01:00:58.321 --> 01:00:59.781
- What do you think?
- [music concludes]

01:00:59.865 --> 01:01:02.117
Do you think she'll fall for me?

01:01:03.410 --> 01:01:04.536
What the heck?

01:01:04.619 --> 01:01:06.580
What do you think? I was rehearsing.

01:01:07.539 --> 01:01:08.832
To ask her out.

01:01:09.875 --> 01:01:12.836
Were you messing with me?
I almost punched you.

01:01:12.919 --> 01:01:14.713
Look at these goosebumps.

01:01:14.796 --> 01:01:16.381
You actually bought it?

01:01:16.464 --> 01:01:19.134
- I'm not crazy, dude.
- You scared me.

01:01:23.513 --> 01:01:24.931
So who do you like?

01:01:25.932 --> 01:01:27.267
[pensive music playing]

01:01:27.350 --> 01:01:29.895
- [Gyeong-gu] What?
- Who are you rehearsing for?

01:01:32.606 --> 01:01:33.481
Oh…

01:01:33.982 --> 01:01:35.233
Wait. Don't tell me.

01:01:36.693 --> 01:01:38.695
It's Mi-ji, right?

01:01:41.031 --> 01:01:43.116
- Yes.
- I knew it.

01:01:43.200 --> 01:01:45.619
You two always hang out together.
It was obvious.

01:01:45.702 --> 01:01:47.204
[Gyeong-gu] I guess.

01:01:47.287 --> 01:01:49.623
But seriously, you can't do it like that.

01:01:49.706 --> 01:01:51.291
- What?
- If you're going to do it,

01:01:51.374 --> 01:01:53.043
you've got to go big and bold.

01:01:53.126 --> 01:01:54.211
Right.

01:01:54.878 --> 01:01:57.005
I'll coach you.

01:01:57.088 --> 01:01:58.548
Try again and do it right.

01:01:58.632 --> 01:02:01.176
- Okay.
- All right. Let's do this.

01:02:01.801 --> 01:02:03.553
- Should we do it here?
- [Gyeong-gu] Here?

01:02:03.637 --> 01:02:05.764
[Seung-hyeon] Where else?
Say, "Mi-ji, I like you."

01:02:05.847 --> 01:02:08.558
- [Gyeong-gu] In broad daylight?
- [Seung-hyeon] Just do it!

01:02:09.100 --> 01:02:10.393
[Gyeong-gu] Mi-ji, I like you.

01:02:11.228 --> 01:02:12.562
[sighs]

01:02:14.147 --> 01:02:15.106
[Ho-su] Gyeong-gu.

01:02:15.190 --> 01:02:16.441
Holy cow!

01:02:17.609 --> 01:02:19.027
- [sighs]
- [music fades]

01:02:19.527 --> 01:02:20.695
What is it?

01:02:21.196 --> 01:02:22.405
Do you really like Mi-ji?

01:02:23.198 --> 01:02:24.991
- What?
- As more than a friend?

01:02:25.867 --> 01:02:27.035
Do you like her?

01:02:31.539 --> 01:02:32.540
Yes.

01:02:33.959 --> 01:02:35.085
Why do you ask?

01:02:35.168 --> 01:02:36.544
Then don't do it.

01:02:37.837 --> 01:02:39.005
Don't tell her.

01:02:39.589 --> 01:02:40.632
Just don't.

01:02:41.591 --> 01:02:43.260
[pensive music playing]

01:02:43.343 --> 01:02:44.594
[running footsteps]

01:02:44.678 --> 01:02:46.471
[student] Gyeong-gu, what are you doing?

01:02:46.554 --> 01:02:48.139
Let's get ready for the big moment.

01:02:48.223 --> 01:02:49.599
Hurry!

01:02:49.683 --> 01:02:51.059
Okay, coming.

01:03:00.860 --> 01:03:03.571
- [music fades]
- Mi-ji, I like you. Go out with me.

01:03:04.698 --> 01:03:07.242
Don't wimp out! Man up and say it.

01:03:07.325 --> 01:03:09.119
Bring out more emotion.

01:03:09.202 --> 01:03:11.329
- [Gyeong-gu exhales]
- Try again.

01:03:11.413 --> 01:03:14.291
[Gyeong-su] Mi-ji, I like you.
Go out with me.

01:03:14.374 --> 01:03:16.126
- You mean like that?
- Hey.

01:03:16.209 --> 01:03:17.377
- Mi-ji's here.
- Shoot.

01:03:17.460 --> 01:03:19.629
- [Gyeong-gu] What? I mean…
- Hurry, quick!

01:03:19.713 --> 01:03:20.922
Now's your chance!

01:03:23.008 --> 01:03:24.134
Screw it!

01:03:30.223 --> 01:03:31.391
[clears throat]

01:03:32.392 --> 01:03:33.393
Mi-ji.

01:03:34.561 --> 01:03:35.895
I like you.

01:03:37.314 --> 01:03:38.606
Go out with me.

01:03:42.652 --> 01:03:43.862
Fine.

01:03:43.945 --> 01:03:46.072
[Seung-hyeon] Look at her face.
Let's see that again.

01:03:46.156 --> 01:03:48.408
- Gosh.
- [group laughs]

01:03:48.491 --> 01:03:50.201
This is hilarious.

01:03:50.285 --> 01:03:51.745
He actually did it.

01:03:51.828 --> 01:03:53.371
So Mi-ji has no idea about him?

01:03:53.455 --> 01:03:55.457
[Seung-hyeon]
She'll figure it out eventually.

01:03:55.540 --> 01:03:58.752
Who knows.
They might stay together for a long time.

01:03:58.835 --> 01:04:00.920
Mi-ji kind of has a boyish vibe.

01:04:01.004 --> 01:04:03.131
- [group laughs]
- [soft daring music playing]

01:04:03.214 --> 01:04:04.424
[Seung-hyeon] Oh man…

01:04:19.898 --> 01:04:21.900
[music intensifies]

01:04:21.983 --> 01:04:23.151
[student 1] There's a fight!

01:04:23.234 --> 01:04:25.403
[students clamoring]

01:04:27.322 --> 01:04:28.448
[student 2] Stop it, you two!

01:04:28.531 --> 01:04:31.201
- [student 3] Shouldn't we break it up?
- [student 4] What?

01:04:32.535 --> 01:04:34.996
- [student 3] Cut it out!
- [student 4] That's enough.

01:04:35.080 --> 01:04:36.831
- Knock it off!
- Calm down.

01:04:36.915 --> 01:04:38.792
- You're way too worked up.
- Enough.

01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:40.001
Stop it.

01:04:50.929 --> 01:04:53.932
- [students murmuring]
- [music turns pensive]

01:04:55.809 --> 01:04:56.976
[pensive music continues]

01:04:57.060 --> 01:04:58.144
Oh.

01:04:59.020 --> 01:05:00.063
Gosh.

01:05:01.856 --> 01:05:03.441
I had no idea.

01:05:03.525 --> 01:05:05.860
I just thought you were her ex.

01:05:07.529 --> 01:05:08.988
Wait, does Mi-ji…

01:05:09.072 --> 01:05:10.532
Of course she knows.

01:05:10.615 --> 01:05:12.951
That's why I could tell it was you.

01:05:13.034 --> 01:05:15.745
I told Mi-ji the truth
right after we started dating.

01:05:15.829 --> 01:05:17.747
I was going to tell her anyway,

01:05:18.248 --> 01:05:21.584
but Ho-su just kept giving me
death stares.

01:05:22.127 --> 01:05:24.671
- [music fades]
- It was just like today.

01:05:24.754 --> 01:05:27.674
He suddenly charged over and asked
if I thought it was funny.

01:05:27.757 --> 01:05:29.050
[chuckles]

01:05:29.134 --> 01:05:31.886
So Ho-su knew everything?

01:05:32.554 --> 01:05:34.597
[chuckles] He never said anything to you?

01:05:35.723 --> 01:05:38.393
Then that bastard was acting
clueless the whole time.

01:05:38.476 --> 01:05:41.187
He's always been creepy like that.

01:05:41.271 --> 01:05:43.064
And he's been fooling you for ten years!

01:05:43.148 --> 01:05:46.067
I'm glad you finally found out, Mi-rae.

01:05:46.985 --> 01:05:48.778
But you knew the whole time too.

01:05:48.862 --> 01:05:50.572
I mean… [scoffs]

01:05:51.156 --> 01:05:53.199
It's not really about who knew what.

01:05:53.283 --> 01:05:54.826
The whole thing is Gyeong-gu's fault.

01:05:54.909 --> 01:05:56.411
Can't you see?

01:05:56.494 --> 01:05:59.414
He's still pretending to be with Mi-ji
after all these years.

01:05:59.497 --> 01:06:03.001
He says they've been together
for ten years now.

01:06:03.084 --> 01:06:05.086
- [laughs]
- [indistinct chatter]

01:06:05.170 --> 01:06:08.840
Wait, don't tell me
Mi-ji still doesn't know.

01:06:08.923 --> 01:06:10.508
Isn't that kind of a scam--

01:06:10.592 --> 01:06:13.052
- Hey!
- [chatter stops]

01:06:13.136 --> 01:06:14.137
[Mi-ji sighs]

01:06:14.220 --> 01:06:15.472
[Seung-hyeon] I mean…

01:06:17.765 --> 01:06:21.269
The 28th student council president
of Duson High, Choi Seung-hyeon.

01:06:21.352 --> 01:06:24.481
I get that it's your biggest
achievement in life,

01:06:24.564 --> 01:06:26.566
but maybe it's time to graduate.

01:06:26.649 --> 01:06:28.818
How are you still
in your high school phase?

01:06:28.902 --> 01:06:29.986
[scoffs]

01:06:30.069 --> 01:06:31.905
- Mi-rae, you--
- I swear, I'll punch you!

01:06:31.988 --> 01:06:34.324
You should be thankful that I'm Mi-rae.

01:06:34.407 --> 01:06:37.494
If I were you, I'd stay away from Mi-ji
starting next week.

01:06:38.077 --> 01:06:39.621
- [Seung-hyeon] Wait…
- Get out of my face!

01:06:39.704 --> 01:06:42.499
[daring music playing]

01:06:42.582 --> 01:06:43.583
[Mi-ji] Shoot…

01:06:55.720 --> 01:06:57.514
[sighs, pants]

01:06:59.807 --> 01:07:02.060
- [panting]
- [daring music continues]

01:07:04.103 --> 01:07:06.397
[Mi-ji yelps, groans]

01:07:07.565 --> 01:07:08.608
[groans]

01:07:12.862 --> 01:07:14.197
[dial tone ringing]

01:07:17.617 --> 01:07:19.994
[cell phone buzzing]

01:07:22.830 --> 01:07:24.374
[music fades]

01:07:24.457 --> 01:07:25.583
Hello.

01:07:26.417 --> 01:07:27.794
Ho-su, where are you?

01:07:27.877 --> 01:07:29.128
I'm in the parking lot.

01:07:29.212 --> 01:07:31.422
Then just stay there for a sec.

01:07:31.506 --> 01:07:32.715
I need to talk to you.

01:07:33.216 --> 01:07:35.593
- About what?
- I'll be right there.

01:07:37.929 --> 01:07:40.014
- [cell phone beeps]
- What? What's going on?

01:07:41.140 --> 01:07:43.226
Mi-rae wants to see me for a minute.

01:07:43.893 --> 01:07:46.646
- You can go.
- No, it's fine.

01:07:46.729 --> 01:07:48.606
You can talk to her. I'll wait.

01:07:49.274 --> 01:07:51.484
No, don't wait for me. You can go.

01:07:57.448 --> 01:07:59.075
Who are you going to go see?

01:08:03.162 --> 01:08:04.372
She's not Mi-rae.

01:08:05.498 --> 01:08:06.499
It's Mi-ji.

01:08:11.254 --> 01:08:12.422
I know.

01:08:12.922 --> 01:08:14.132
What?

01:08:15.091 --> 01:08:16.342
I know

01:08:17.093 --> 01:08:18.428
that it's Mi-ji.

01:08:23.433 --> 01:08:25.602
- Sorry.
- [soft uplifting music playing]

01:08:25.685 --> 01:08:26.978
I have to go.

01:08:39.657 --> 01:08:41.951
[soft uplifting music continues]

01:09:02.722 --> 01:09:04.390
[mumbling] Ho-su.

01:09:06.809 --> 01:09:10.104
I don't want to lie to you.

01:09:12.899 --> 01:09:14.734
The truth is,

01:09:15.443 --> 01:09:17.195
- I'm Mi…
- [music concludes]

01:09:17.278 --> 01:09:19.155
[Mi-ji] No, stop.

01:09:19.238 --> 01:09:21.783
Don't say it. No.

01:09:22.283 --> 01:09:23.534
Don't.

01:09:24.327 --> 01:09:26.412
But I feel uneasy.

01:09:27.455 --> 01:09:28.790
Uneasy.

01:09:31.334 --> 01:09:32.669
[Mi-ji groans]

01:09:34.170 --> 01:09:35.588
[groans]

01:09:41.552 --> 01:09:44.180
[tender music playing]

01:10:21.759 --> 01:10:22.844
Good night.

01:10:23.720 --> 01:10:24.762
Mi-ji.

01:10:25.847 --> 01:10:27.098
[Mi-ji] Okay.

01:10:38.067 --> 01:10:39.193
Mi-ji.

01:10:39.277 --> 01:10:40.486
[Mi-ji] Yes?

01:10:45.867 --> 01:10:47.118
Mi-ji.

01:10:47.660 --> 01:10:51.497
Why do you keep calling me?

01:10:52.373 --> 01:10:54.000
[music concludes]

01:10:54.542 --> 01:10:57.044
[gentle pop song playing]

01:10:58.963 --> 01:11:01.799
[in English]
♪ We used to draw the city lights… ♪

01:11:01.883 --> 01:11:04.761
[Ho-su in Korean] People always
have a reason for hiding things.

01:11:04.844 --> 01:11:06.179
What shoes?

01:11:07.138 --> 01:11:09.015
Don't act like you don't know.

01:11:09.098 --> 01:11:11.726
Ah, the shoes. Right.

01:11:11.809 --> 01:11:15.229
Why is there always a line at that place?

01:11:15.313 --> 01:11:16.314
[Ji-yun] What?

01:11:16.981 --> 01:11:20.067
That place was only on Jeju.
I guess they opened one here.

01:11:20.151 --> 01:11:22.487
- [song continues]
- [singing in Korean]

01:11:22.570 --> 01:11:25.698
[in English]
♪ I don't wanna wait forever ♪

01:11:27.742 --> 01:11:31.078
♪ To tell you
What's been growing stronger… ♪

01:11:31.704 --> 01:11:32.872
[Ho-su in Korean] We all have

01:11:32.955 --> 01:11:34.624
that one question
we don't want to be asked.

01:11:34.707 --> 01:11:38.461
Does choosing not to ask it
count as being deceitful?

01:11:38.544 --> 01:11:42.590
- [song continues]
- [singing in Korean]

01:11:44.091 --> 01:11:49.472
[singing in Korean continues]

01:11:49.555 --> 01:11:51.516
Oh? Ho-su.

01:11:52.308 --> 01:11:54.477
[panting]

01:11:54.560 --> 01:11:57.522
[in English] ♪ I am with you ♪

01:12:08.491 --> 01:12:11.577
[song concludes]

01:12:13.037 --> 01:12:16.541
[in Korean] You two got guts.
I'll give you that.

01:12:19.377 --> 01:12:21.212
Is everything okay with Mi-ji?

01:12:22.421 --> 01:12:24.090
Let's hope so.

01:12:25.508 --> 01:12:28.261
Are you going to tell anyone?

01:12:28.344 --> 01:12:29.971
Who would I tell?

01:12:30.054 --> 01:12:31.848
Should I go tattle to your mom?

01:12:33.641 --> 01:12:35.726
Things like this
are just meant to stay secret.

01:12:35.810 --> 01:12:37.353
So stop talking nonsense.

01:12:39.522 --> 01:12:41.482
If you're going to do it, do it right.

01:12:41.566 --> 01:12:44.652
Your mom thinks you're Mi-ji,
and she's really worried sick.

01:12:44.735 --> 01:12:46.445
You should go out more.

01:12:46.529 --> 01:12:48.990
Why did you suddenly quit
the strawberry farm?

01:12:50.658 --> 01:12:51.742
Did he…

01:12:52.493 --> 01:12:53.744
hire someone new?

01:12:53.828 --> 01:12:55.872
How would I know?

01:12:55.955 --> 01:12:57.373
He didn't say anything.

01:12:58.332 --> 01:13:01.335
Why? Do you regret it now?
Hard to let go of that daily pay?

01:13:01.836 --> 01:13:02.962
[sighs]

01:13:03.546 --> 01:13:04.839
Maybe.

01:13:04.922 --> 01:13:06.090
[grunts]

01:13:07.508 --> 01:13:09.385
Where do you want to go?

01:13:09.468 --> 01:13:10.845
Do you want to go home,

01:13:10.928 --> 01:13:13.472
or check out some other place
since we're in Seoul?

01:13:20.146 --> 01:13:21.272
[sighs]

01:13:21.355 --> 01:13:23.399
I don't really have anywhere to go.

01:13:30.615 --> 01:13:32.909
Why are you limping? Did you get hurt?

01:13:33.492 --> 01:13:35.786
[Mi-ji] I ran
and twisted my ankle earlier.

01:13:35.870 --> 01:13:36.996
It's fine.

01:13:37.914 --> 01:13:39.707
Ah. Get on my back.

01:13:40.750 --> 01:13:43.252
Come on, don't be ridiculous.

01:13:43.336 --> 01:13:46.797
- It's okay. Let me.
- Seriously, I'm fine.

01:13:47.715 --> 01:13:50.801
What? Are you afraid?
That I'll break my leg carrying you?

01:13:51.510 --> 01:13:53.596
No, it's not that…

01:13:53.679 --> 01:13:56.807
I've been in physical therapy
for 15 years. I can handle it.

01:13:56.891 --> 01:13:59.518
My leg is in better shape
than your ankle right now.

01:14:01.854 --> 01:14:02.855
Hop on.

01:14:04.231 --> 01:14:05.358
Oh…

01:14:07.902 --> 01:14:09.153
Come on.

01:14:10.863 --> 01:14:13.032
[tender music playing]

01:14:19.747 --> 01:14:22.708
[Mi-ji] Why did you act
like you didn't know?

01:14:22.792 --> 01:14:23.793
About what?

01:14:24.418 --> 01:14:26.003
[Mi-ji] Gyeong-gu.

01:14:26.087 --> 01:14:28.255
You knew all along, right?

01:14:28.881 --> 01:14:32.885
If you knew Mi-ji and Gyeong-gu
weren't a thing, why haven't you…

01:14:32.969 --> 01:14:35.221
I'm a bit shady, you know.

01:14:35.304 --> 01:14:37.723
Come on, don't say that.

01:14:38.891 --> 01:14:40.893
It's not like I know everything.

01:14:41.394 --> 01:14:43.604
Just because
I found out something by chance

01:14:43.688 --> 01:14:45.898
doesn't mean I know
what's between those two.

01:14:48.025 --> 01:14:49.819
Don't you ever feel it's unfair?

01:14:50.695 --> 01:14:52.613
You keep secrets that aren't even yours,

01:14:52.697 --> 01:14:55.866
and in return, you miss out,
lose out, and get misunderstood.

01:14:55.950 --> 01:14:57.326
You do so much for others,

01:14:57.410 --> 01:14:59.870
and all you get in return
is being called "shady."

01:15:00.621 --> 01:15:02.456
I don't do it for others.

01:15:04.458 --> 01:15:06.836
I can't comfort people
or fix their problems.

01:15:08.045 --> 01:15:09.088
But…

01:15:10.256 --> 01:15:12.341
I can keep a secret.

01:15:13.384 --> 01:15:15.886
[scoffs] You're such a fool.

01:15:17.930 --> 01:15:21.058
Anyway, what was it
you wanted to tell me earlier?

01:15:22.143 --> 01:15:23.644
Oh, that…

01:15:25.187 --> 01:15:29.483
I was actually planning
to tell you next week,

01:15:30.526 --> 01:15:35.114
but it's not just about me,
so it's a bit tricky.

01:15:35.197 --> 01:15:38.576
Still, I thought I should tell you…

01:15:38.659 --> 01:15:40.119
Just tell me later.

01:15:40.995 --> 01:15:42.038
What?

01:15:42.121 --> 01:15:43.622
Whatever it is,

01:15:44.915 --> 01:15:48.836
tell me when you feel comfortable talking.

01:15:58.888 --> 01:16:01.223
[Mi-ji] Just like the moon that follows me

01:16:01.307 --> 01:16:03.434
without ever being noticed,

01:16:04.727 --> 01:16:06.854
this fool has been silently waiting,

01:16:07.438 --> 01:16:10.024
for who knows how long.

01:16:11.484 --> 01:16:14.320
I liked Ho-su
and this foolish side of him…

01:16:16.989 --> 01:16:18.324
and I still do.

01:16:23.287 --> 01:16:25.039
[music fades]

01:16:25.122 --> 01:16:26.916
- [grunting]
- [thunder crashing]

01:16:31.212 --> 01:16:32.505
[pants]

01:16:36.675 --> 01:16:39.345
[grunts] Gosh, please!

01:16:40.888 --> 01:16:42.181
[clattering]

01:16:55.444 --> 01:16:57.905
Fuck, stop already!

01:16:58.489 --> 01:17:00.533
There's nothing left now!

01:17:01.075 --> 01:17:03.911
[screams]

01:17:03.994 --> 01:17:06.163
[sobs, cries]

01:17:08.374 --> 01:17:10.501
[Mi-rae shouting] What are you doing here?

01:17:13.379 --> 01:17:16.298
[uplifting music playing]

01:17:24.473 --> 01:17:25.850
Grandpa?

01:17:35.818 --> 01:17:37.069
Get up.

01:17:37.153 --> 01:17:38.696
How did you…

01:17:39.488 --> 01:17:41.365
We can talk later.

01:17:41.448 --> 01:17:42.825
Get up now.

01:17:43.492 --> 01:17:50.457
CHANGHWA FARM

01:17:52.168 --> 01:17:54.753
- [music fades]
- [thunder rumbling, crashing]

01:17:54.837 --> 01:17:56.088
[Se-jin sighs]

01:17:57.339 --> 01:18:01.010
You showed up like a superhero,
so I figured you'd know what to do.

01:18:01.510 --> 01:18:02.887
But you're just as lost.

01:18:02.970 --> 01:18:05.389
Jeez. I came to help, you know.

01:18:06.891 --> 01:18:07.766
Sorry.

01:18:07.850 --> 01:18:09.894
I'm thankful, really.

01:18:11.020 --> 01:18:13.772
But now what?
The roads are flooded. You can't go home.

01:18:15.733 --> 01:18:17.818
I'll sleep over here tonight, so you can…

01:18:17.902 --> 01:18:19.111
[light fizzing]

01:18:20.654 --> 01:18:22.072
[thunder crashes]

01:18:23.407 --> 01:18:24.366
[Se-jin] That was scary.

01:18:24.450 --> 01:18:25.618
[lighter clicking]

01:18:25.701 --> 01:18:27.119
[rain pattering]

01:18:31.207 --> 01:18:32.708
[inhales deeply]

01:18:37.880 --> 01:18:40.382
Seriously? A blackout?

01:18:40.466 --> 01:18:41.884
Did you call home?

01:18:42.426 --> 01:18:45.387
I already told Mom
I wouldn't be home tonight.

01:18:47.014 --> 01:18:50.935
I wasn't planning to come here, though.

01:18:52.394 --> 01:18:55.314
This is only going to fuel the rumors.

01:18:55.898 --> 01:18:57.316
We're screwed.

01:18:58.525 --> 01:18:59.777
[Mi-rae grunts]

01:19:01.987 --> 01:19:03.447
Seriously, why did you come?

01:19:06.242 --> 01:19:09.203
My friend said he could take me
anywhere I wanted,

01:19:10.287 --> 01:19:12.498
but this was the only place
I could think of.

01:19:13.040 --> 01:19:14.041
Why?

01:19:16.710 --> 01:19:18.504
Because what's out there is fake,

01:19:19.296 --> 01:19:20.923
and this place is real.

01:19:21.006 --> 01:19:22.091
At least to me.

01:19:24.343 --> 01:19:26.470
Then why do you hate the rumors so much?

01:19:29.431 --> 01:19:31.058
There's no reason to like them.

01:19:33.227 --> 01:19:34.186
[theme song playing]

01:19:34.270 --> 01:19:35.521
I like them.

01:19:36.063 --> 01:19:37.439
The rumors about us.

01:19:39.525 --> 01:19:40.776
[in English] ♪ You're driving ♪

01:19:40.859 --> 01:19:43.362
- ♪ Alone at night ♪
- [thunder crashing]

01:19:44.238 --> 01:19:47.700
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

01:19:48.659 --> 01:19:55.541
[singing in Korean]

01:19:57.876 --> 01:20:01.380
♪ And you're feeling all alone ♪

01:20:02.214 --> 01:20:05.718
♪ When you're staying up all night ♪

01:20:06.760 --> 01:20:13.225
[singing in Korean]

01:20:13.309 --> 01:20:14.476
YU MI-JI

01:20:14.560 --> 01:20:18.272
Do you even know
what Mi-rae's going through at work?

01:20:18.355 --> 01:20:20.566
Use it to help the people
who are important to you.

01:20:20.649 --> 01:20:24.111
There's even a novel based
on the public takeover bid for Hyudi Bio.

01:20:24.194 --> 01:20:26.530
[Se-jin] So you're not quiet.
You just chose not to talk.

01:20:26.613 --> 01:20:29.033
- Ever considered working in finance?
- What?

01:20:29.116 --> 01:20:30.993
- Ms. Seoul?
- That 200,000 won-a-day job?

01:20:31.076 --> 01:20:33.537
[Se-jin] Since we've run into each other,
let's go eat together.

01:20:33.620 --> 01:20:35.914
[Ji-yun]
Mi-rae didn't tell you about the rumors?

01:20:35.998 --> 01:20:39.168
She threw a fit at Mi-rae
in the company lobby.

01:20:39.251 --> 01:20:40.753
[woman] Why are you still here?

01:20:40.836 --> 01:20:41.920
That's disappointing.

01:20:42.004 --> 01:20:44.548
I haven't gone a day
without thinking about you, Ms. Yu.

01:20:44.631 --> 01:20:50.012
- [song continues]
- [singing in Korean]

01:20:50.596 --> 01:20:52.639
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
